INSERT INTO `quest_request_items` VALUES
(2,1,0,'Yes, mighty $C, I sensed your arrival. I trust you have more news to report to me about your hunt?',15595),
(5,1,0,'Oh, a shipment from my brother? Splendid! Fortune truly shines on me today!',15595),
(9,1,0,'Ah, I see you\'re back! I hope you\'ve been hard at work clearing those fields of those Harvest Watchers. Have you killed twenty yet?',15595),
(10,6,0,'Well, what news do you have?  You look like you\'ve been in quite the fight... is Scrimshank alive?',15595),
(11,1,0,'Hail, $N. Have you been killing Gnolls...?',15595),
(12,1,0,'Perhaps I did not make myself clear, pledge. In order to prove your worth as a servant to The People\'s Militia and to the Light you need to slay 15 Defias Trappers and 15 Defias Smugglers then return to me when the deed is done.',15595),
(13,1,0,'We have not time to talk, $N. The Defias Pillagers are denying the people of Westfall the peace and prosperity they deserve. Make sure at least 15 Defias Pillagers and 15 Defias Looters have been killed. That will send a clear message that corruption is not welcome here.',15595),
(14,1,66,'$N, now is no time for idle chatter. If you still wish to prove yourself to The People\'s Militia you need to slay the Defias I notified you about earlier. Return to me when you have completed your duty.',15595),
(16,1,0,'Farming is thirsty work, and I\'m always looking for refreshing spring water.$B$BIf you have any, then I\'m willing to make a trade.',15595),
(19,1,0,'Orc pressure from Blackrock is still tense. But have you at least rid us of Tharil\'zun?',15595),
(20,1,0,'Have you been slaying orcs, $N? If so, then show me...',15595),
(22,5,4,'All I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!',15595),
(23,1,0,'Ah - $N - I was just thinking about you! How goes your hunting?',15595),
(24,1,0,'Greetings once again, $N! Have you come to show me proof of your hunt?',15595),
(25,1,0,'You back already? What\'s the situation out there - all cleared up now, thanks to you?',15595),
(32,1,0,'I\'m sorry. I don\'t know you... but from the look of things you have at least heard something of me. Now, what can I help you with? Do you have something for me?',15595),
(34,1,4,'Is Bellygrub still at it or were you able to rid Lakeshire of the pest once and for all?',15595),
(35,1,0,NULL,15595),
(36,1,0,'I\'m going to miss that Verna Furlbrow so much. I don\'t suppose you happened to see her on your way here?',15595),
(37,1,0,NULL,15595),
(38,1,0,'Come back with the following ingredients: $b $b 3 Stringy Vulture Meat $b 3 Goretusk Snouts $b 3 Murloc Eyes $b 3 Okra',15595),
(39,1,0,NULL,15595),
(40,1,0,NULL,15595),
(45,1,0,NULL,15595),
(46,1,0,'How goes the hunting, $N?',15595),
(47,1,0,'Psst! You have that Gold Dust for me...for me?',15595),
(48,1,0,'Hiccup! Ho ho! You want an encore?$B$BIn the land to the south where vines twist and creep$BLies a hidden well where the water runs deep$BPure as the Light\'s sacred Daughter$BBring to me now some Holy Spring Water.',15595),
(49,1,0,'Encore? Well, sure!$B$BAmber is the hue of my life\'s longest love$BLike the last embers of dusk in the sky above$BRetrieve for me so that my love shall be born$BOne sack of each: barley, rye and corn.',15595),
(50,1,0,'An encore for you? Well sure friend!$B$BI\'ll mix and mix till we have a mash$BFor this will be our own private stash$BA still must be fashioned of metal strong$BBring me some Truesilver so I can finish this song.',15595),
(51,1,0,'An encore? Why for you, anything!$B$BNot yet filtered but freshly distilled$BLike unseeded land waiting there tilled.$BNext I will fashion our pile of charcoal$BDeliver a sycamore branch, that is your next goal.',15595),
(52,1,0,'Have you killed those wolves and bears?',15595),
(53,1,0,'Sure, I\'ll sing it again for you, friend!$B$BMellifluous liquid clear as a baby\'s tears$BTurns a lovely deep amber over the years$BBut before we proceed to get lit to the hilt$BA barrel of charred oak must be built.',15595),
(54,1,0,'You have word from McBride?  Northshire is a garden compared to Elwynn Forest, but I wonder what Marshal McBride has to report.$B$BHere, let me have his papers...',15595),
(55,1,0,'Is Morbent Fel defeated?!',15595),
(56,1,21,'Have you killed those warriors and mages?',15595),
(57,1,21,'Return to me once you have killed 15 Skeletal Fiends and 15 Skeletal Horrors, $N.',15595),
(58,1,66,'I need your assistance, $N. Travel to the cemetery to the northwest and rid the eastern mausoleum of 20 Plague Spreaders.$B$BReturn to me when your task is complete.',15595),
(59,1,0,'I have been commissioned by the Stormwind Army to supply their people with cloth and leather armor.$b$bIf you have a marker for me, then I\'d be happy to make you something.',15595),
(60,1,0,'Did you gather those candles yet?',15595),
(61,1,0,'Oh, a shipment from my brother? Splendid! Fortune truly shines on me today!',15595),
(62,1,0,'What do you have to report, $N? Have you been to the Fargodeep Mine?',15595),
(64,1,0,'Don\'t suppose you were able to get my watch?',15595),
(65,1,0,NULL,15595),
(66,1,0,NULL,15595),
(67,1,0,NULL,15595),
(68,1,0,'Ah, I remember you. You\'re the one who was asking about that Stalvan fellow. Did you ever find what you were looking for?',15595),
(69,1,0,NULL,15595),
(70,1,0,'What have ya got there? Let me take a look at that. . .',15595),
(71,1,0,'Hello, $N. Have you discovered the fates of Rolf and Malakai?',15595),
(72,1,0,NULL,15595),
(74,6,0,'What have you got there? I cannot see. My eyesight is very bad. Put it in my hands.',15595),
(75,6,0,'Did you find that page I mentioned, $N?',15595),
(76,1,0,'Hail, $N. What do you have to report? Have you scouted the Jasperlode Mine?',15595),
(77,6,0,'I trust that your arrival here at our camp is to deliver the bottles of ripple that are integral to the task at hand, yes?',15595),
(78,6,5,'Marshal Haggard sent you? Why didn\'t you say so?$B$BAh, good ol\' Haggard. Poor chap is going to be completely blind before long. Anyway, let me see what you\'ve got there.',15595),
(79,1,0,'This better be good, $C. Let me see what you have and tell me your tale. But by the Light, be quick about it. Darkshire\'s defense is my number one priority. I have not the time to squander on dead-end leads.',15595),
(80,1,5,'Back again, $N? What do you have this time?',15595),
(81,1,0,'If you\'re not here to buy anything, and you\'re not here to deliver anything, then you\'re wasting my time! You better have that ripple!',15595),
(82,1,0,'You\'re Junior Surveyor $N, yes? Quickly now, there is a dire situation at hand! Do you have the insect parts that Fizzledowser said you would?!',15595),
(83,1,0,'I\'m running low on linen, $N. Do you have any for me?',15595),
(84,1,0,'Ugh... I\'m starving! Do you have that pie for me, $N?',15595),
(85,1,0,NULL,15595),
(86,1,0,'I don\'t think it\'s right feeding the boy who stole my necklace in the first place, but if that\'s what it takes to get back what\'s mine, then so be it!$b$bDo you have that boar meat?',15595),
(87,1,0,'Hello, $N. Have you found my necklace?',15595),
(88,1,0,'Did you see her yet? Did you get her?',15595),
(89,1,0,'This bridge isn\'t going to build itself! Now where are those iron pikes and iron rivets?',15595),
(90,1,2,'Were you able to find 10 Lean Wolf Flanks yet? How about the herbs from Felicia in Stormwind?',15595),
(91,1,0,'Turn in 10 Shadowhide Pendants to me, and you shall be rewarded.',15595),
(92,1,0,'I still need five pieces of Tough Condor Meat, five Great Goretusk Snouts and five helpings of Crisp Spider Meat.',15595),
(93,1,0,'Hail, $N. Did you get those Gooey Spider Legs yet?',15595),
(94,1,0,'This Lion Statue has sat here for decades, and keeps a lonely watch over the infamous Tower of Ilgalar.$B$BThere is a depression at the base of the statue, where a gem or glyph might be set...',15595),
(95,1,0,NULL,15595),
(97,1,5,'Yes, $N?',15595),
(98,1,0,'Yes, $N?',15595),
(99,1,0,'Have you secured the Pyrewood Shackles yet, $N?',15595),
(101,1,0,'Bring to me 10 ghoul fangs, 10 skeleton fingers and 5 vials of spider venom. For you I shall enchant a Totem of Infliction which will harm those who attempt violent acts against you.',15595),
(102,1,0,'Have you collected 8 paws from those treacherous Gnolls yet?',15595),
(103,1,0,'The flame will not burn for long without oil, $N.',15595),
(104,1,0,'Have you laid waste to the menace known as Old Murk-Eye yet? He has been spotted roaming the coastline of Westfall.$B$BReturn to me when the foul beast is dead.',15595),
(105,1,0,'Your task has been given to you, $N. Do you have a shard from the lich\'s phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?',15595),
(106,1,0,'You have what?? Maybell is the light of my dull life. Hurry, let me see her letter!',15595),
(107,1,0,'You have a note from \"Gramma\" Stonefield, eh? I haven\'t seen Mildred in years! I wonder what she has to say...',15595),
(109,1,0,'An... Any luck??',15595),
(110,1,0,NULL,15595),
(111,1,0,'I can\'t wait to hear how my friends react!$B$BThey\'ll never expect it',15595),
(112,1,0,'Do you have that crystal kelp? I\'m sure Maybell is anxious to see her beau...',15595),
(113,6,0,'Well Junior Surveyor $n, has ol\' Pestlezugg got that report ready yet?',15595),
(114,1,0,'Did you deliver my letter to Tommy Joe? What did he say??',15595),
(115,1,0,'How goes your conflict with the shadowcasters? Did you find the midnight orbs?',15595),
(116,1,0,'I need you to pick up a keg of Thunderbrew Lager from Grimbooze Thunderbrew in the Westfall hills, a cask of Merlot from Stormwind, a bottle of Moonshine from Darkshire and a skin of Sweet Rum from Goldshire. Bring those back to me and I will see to it you are rewarded.',15595),
(117,1,0,'Hurry, my friend, move with haste $bIn order for our rich lager to taste $bMore like beer and less like stew, $bHops are needed to make the brew.',15595),
(118,1,0,'What\'s that? Verner sent you, you say? Well give me his note. And SPEAK UP!',15595),
(119,1,0,'Great, you\'re back! Did you get the shoes?',15595),
(120,1,0,'What have you there?',15595),
(121,1,0,'Did the General send news? Are reinforcements on the way?',15595),
(122,1,0,'I know that greedy Argus will send someone to collect his scales if I don\'t give them to him soon. Have you found those scales yet?',15595),
(123,0,0,'What?!? We haven\'t had our people working the Elwynn mines for months!$B$BLet me see that note you have...',15595),
(124,1,0,'Yes? Is there something I can do for you?',15595),
(125,1,0,'Were you able to find my tools?',15595),
(126,1,0,'Yowler is a dangerous creature, $N. If you\'re not ready for him, I understand.',15595),
(127,1,0,'You have some sunfish for me, eh?',15595),
(128,1,0,'Return once you have slain 15 Blackrock Champions.',15595),
(129,1,0,'Darcy sent me a lunch, did she? Such a kind heart she has. Well...let\'s have it!',15595),
(130,1,0,NULL,15595),
(131,1,0,'Hello again, $N. Did Parker like the lunch I sent him?',15595),
(132,1,0,'Good to see you back, $N. What did Wiley have to say for himself?',15595),
(133,1,0,'I think I hear a pack of Ghouls scurrying around the back of the house - I better put that effigy up quick! Did you get those Ghoul Ribs for me?',15595),
(134,1,0,'Do you have my crate? If so, then please...give it to me quickly!',15595),
(135,1,0,'What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man. . .',15595),
(136,1,0,NULL,15595),
(138,1,0,NULL,15595),
(139,1,0,NULL,15595),
(140,1,0,NULL,15595),
(141,1,0,'Did Master Shaw shed any light on things?',15595),
(142,1,0,'$N, were you able to gather any information? Did you locate the messenger?',15595),
(143,1,0,'Hail, $C. What business do you have with The People\'s Militia?',15595),
(144,1,0,'Shall we expect the People\'s Militia soon? Does Lord Stoutmantle\'s news bode well?',15595),
(145,1,0,'You appear to have traveled from afar, $C. What business do you have here in Darkshire?',15595),
(146,1,0,'Ah, good to see you back, messenger. Shall I inform the Marshal that the Night Watch is on its way from Darkshire?',15595),
(147,1,0,'Did you find the Collector? Did you discover whom he\'s working for?',15595),
(148,1,0,NULL,15595),
(149,1,0,'Oh please, don\'t look at me! I tore out these eyes with my own hands, but I can still feel your gaze!$B$BI\'m hideous! Hideous! Please, look away!!',15595),
(150,1,0,'Do you have those fins? Hurry, we need those murlocs driven from the lake!',15595),
(151,1,0,'Old Blanchy is on her last leg. Did you happen to find any oats for her?',15595),
(152,1,0,'Kill 7 Tidehunters, 7 Warriors, 7 Oracles and 7 Coastrunners and I will see to it that you are rewarded.',15595),
(153,1,0,'Bring me 15 red leather bandanas and I\'ll pay you well.',15595),
(154,1,0,'I sense that you have seen Blind Mary. You have my Comb...?',15595),
(155,1,0,'What business do you have with me? I am a very busy man...',15595),
(156,6,2,'Hi, $N. You have that rot blossoms for me yet?',15595),
(157,1,0,'I need to string the Ghost Hair Thread along my door and my windows to keep out unwanted spirits. Did you get it for me?',15595),
(158,1,0,NULL,15595),
(159,1,0,'I need that Zombie Juice to keep me warm on these cold, dark nights. Did you get it for me?',15595),
(160,1,0,'Abercrombie...? I don\'t know a person of that name. You say you have a letter for me from this Abercrombie fellow?$B$BWell let\'s have it then...',15595),
(161,1,0,'You say somethin\', sonny? Can\'t hear a bloody thing besides the ringin\' in me ears. Say, what\'s that you got there?',15595),
(162,2,0,'Peace and tranquility be upon you, stranger.  Why have you sought me out this day?',15595),
(163,1,0,'Ah, $N! Back so soon? No doubt you\'ve been at the hunt again? Don\'t worry if you\'ve had some setbacks, in the long run it will make you better!$B$B...You couldn\'t get much worse, anyway...',15595),
(164,1,0,'You look a sturdy type, $C. Have you come to join our fight?',15595),
(165,1,0,NULL,15595),
(166,1,0,'How goes the hunt for Edwin VanCleef?',15595),
(167,1,0,'Did you find any sign of my brother? Is there any hope after all this time?',15595),
(168,1,0,'Were you able to retrieve any of my old co-worker\'s Miners\' Union Cards?',15595),
(169,1,0,'What do you have there, $R?',15595),
(173,1,0,'$N, how fares the hunt?',15595),
(174,1,0,'Have you found a skilled engineer to create a bronze tube yet?',15595),
(175,1,0,NULL,15595),
(176,1,0,'Yes, Hogger has been a real pain for me and my men. You have something to report about the beast?',15595),
(177,1,0,'I showed Cog the beginnings of our star-viewing machine. He was impressed. Did you happen to find a reflective device?',15595),
(178,1,0,'I spoke to you through a pendant, you say? Hmm...give it to me, so that I might study it.',15595),
(180,1,0,'What news do you bring before the Court?',15595),
(181,1,0,'Were you able to convince Zzarc\'Vul to lend us his monocle for our experiment?',15595),
(182,6,0,'From what I\'ve learned, these trolls hail from the Frostmane clan. I\'m afraid I don\'t know much else about them that would be of any use to you, $N.',15595),
(184,1,0,'You have the deed to my farm?? That\'s good news! Some ruffians stole it days ago... I thought it was gone for good!$b$bPlease, let me have it. We\'re on our way out of Westfall and ain\'t coming back any time soon, but if we do then we\'ll need those papers...',15595),
(185,1,1,'I don\'t feel confident in training you further, $n, until you have proven yourself skilled in slaying the youngest of the tigers first.',15595),
(186,1,0,'If you strive for greater challenges you must first prove yourself with the task at hand. Return to me after you\'ve killed 10 Stranglethorn Tigers.',15595),
(187,1,0,'You must kill 10 Elder Stranglethorn Tigers before I give you the final challenge that will determine if you are a true tiger hunting master.',15595),
(188,6,0,'How goes the hunt?',15595),
(189,6,0,'You\'ve had success I hope? All over the place, those trolls. Filthy devils.$b$bOh yes, that reminds me! Be sure to tell your friends, yes? We could use much assistance!',15595),
(190,1,25,'A true panther hunter would be out in the fields, trying to stalk his prey. Show some commitment to your goal, $c, and get back out there.',15595),
(191,1,0,'Bhag\'thera can prove to be an elusive beast. How fairs the hunt?',15595),
(192,1,0,'Bhag\'thera can prove to be an elusive beast. How fairs the hunt?',15595),
(193,1,0,'You\'re still alive!  Excellent!  How fares the hunt?',15595),
(194,1,0,'I never met a hunter who got any kills by standing around the campfire - well, except for my father. Were you planning on killing those Stranglethorn Raptors or were you hoping they would die of old age?',15595),
(195,1,0,'A true hunter sets his focus on his prey. You, my friend, seem more concerned with chit-chatting around the campfire. Now get out there and kill 10 Lashtails before I go and rid the entire bloody jungle of them in one hunt.',15595),
(196,1,0,'Bah! What are you doing standing around, $N! A true big game hunter never gives up once his prey is in his sights. Those Jungle Stalkers aren\'t going to come running up to this campfire and throw themselves in it. Silly bloke.',15595),
(197,1,0,'Ah, so you\'re hunting Tethis?  Tracked her all the way back to camp, did you?',15595),
(198,1,0,'Yes? What do you want? Oh, supplies from the goblins. Strange seeing a $R delivering them, usually they send their own. No matter... you didn\'t touch them did you? Good good... we wouldn\'t want anything to happen to our mines, oh no.',15595),
(199,1,0,'Did you happen to discover any clues, $N?',15595),
(200,1,0,NULL,15595),
(201,1,6,'Well?  Did you have any luck in locating the camp?',15595),
(202,1,0,'Dare I hope that Kurzen and his defenders are dead, $N?',15595),
(203,1,0,'I hope you\'ve been successful in your hunting, $N. We won\'t last long against him without your help.',15595),
(204,1,0,'I\'m waiting on those remedies and that extract, $N.',15595),
(205,1,0,'Do you have those fetishes, $N? They might hold the secret to Kurzen\'s degradation...I must know!',15595),
(206,0,0,'I give you my blessing. Mai\'Zoth\'s strength is matched only by his evil.',15595),
(207,1,0,'$N! Do you have the troll legends? I must know their secrets!',15595),
(208,1,0,'I see you\'re back, $g old bloke : lass;.  King Bangalash has caused me to come crawling back to camp many times.  Hang in there.',15595),
(209,1,0,'Tough buggers, aren\'t they? Well, have you had any luck? Sorry to seem impatient, but this has been a huge thorn in my side! Well?',15595),
(210,1,0,'Hello! You brought me something?',15595),
(211,6,0,'Your task has been given to you, $N.  Do you have a shard from the lich\'s phylactery as proof of the task being accomplished?',15595),
(212,1,0,'$N! Do you have that haunch? I must begin preparing it soon, or the banquet will be ruined!',15595),
(213,0,0,'I need those stones, $n. By whatever means necessary! Just do it, don\'t give me the details!$b$bIt\'s about results, $n, nothing more, nothing less.',15595),
(214,1,0,'Have you been reclaiming our land from the Defias gang? If so show me 10 Red Silk Bandanas as proof.',15595),
(215,1,0,NULL,15595),
(216,1,6,'Have you taken the fight to the Thistlefur?  With a clear path between our bases, our chances of claiming the whole of Ashenvale increase dramatically.',15595),
(217,1,0,'Grawmug and his two guards, Gnasher and Brawler, are still alive. Your mission is not complete until all 3 have been brought to death. The Dwarven empire is counting on you, $N.',15595),
(218,1,0,'$N! Any luck?',15595),
(219,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(221,1,0,'Back so soon, $N? I hope you haven\'t come to tell me you\'ve given up.',15595),
(222,1,0,'Intimidating beasts aren\'t they? But have no fear, $N, those who stand for the Light will never fall!',15595),
(223,1,0,'Yes, what is it? Make it quick, I\'ve pressing matters to attend to.',15595),
(224,1,0,'Loch Modan is under siege, $N!  We need every able-bodied member of the Alliance to aid our cause.  Have you killed 10 Stonesplinter Troggs and 10 Stonesplinter Scouts yet?',15595),
(225,1,0,NULL,15595),
(226,1,0,'You still hunting wolves...?',15595),
(227,1,0,NULL,15595),
(228,1,0,'I don\'t blame you if you\'re having trouble with him, $N. Some of our strongest Watchers have been lost to Mor\'Ladim.',15595),
(229,1,0,NULL,15595),
(230,1,0,'You found what?? Please, let me see it...',15595),
(231,1,0,'Leave me be...',15595),
(232,6,0,'Yes, and what may I assist you with?  Are you here on business for the Royal Apothecary Society, or have you arrived here merely to brighten my day?',15595),
(235,1,0,NULL,15595),
(236,0,0,'Well? Did you manage to find the embers or did the Horde beat you to it and leave you crying?',15595),
(237,1,0,'We need more time, $r. Your orders are to kill 10 Stonesplinter Skullthumpers and 10 Stonesplinter Seers. Keep the enemy under pressure until we are granted reinforcements. This is no time for idle behavior.',15595),
(238,1,0,'Yes, I think Luca is as disturbing as you do. It matters not - hand me the field sampling kit. I will need to make some adjustments to it in order to survey for the proper base materials.$b$bYou have the kit, don\'t you?',15595),
(239,1,0,NULL,15595),
(240,1,0,'$N, you\'re here! Do you have my food?!?',15595),
(243,1,0,NULL,15595),
(244,1,0,NULL,15595),
(245,1,0,'You\'d best be careful when dealing with the spiders, I\'ve lost a few of my men to them, and trust me, it isn\'t a pleasant sight to see a man hanging upside down in their webs after the venom has started to soften them up.$B$BI wouldn\'t want to see one of the bugs having you for lunch.',15595),
(246,1,0,'Excuse me, $N, but we have a lot to keep our hands tied here. If you have nothing to report, then I must put my mind to other matters.',15595),
(247,1,0,NULL,15595),
(248,1,0,'This jar once held a foul-smelling liquor, but now lies empty and forgotten on a pair of barrels.',15595),
(249,1,0,'Hurry, $N, before my fears of Morganth spreading his power are made real!',15595),
(250,1,0,NULL,15595),
(251,1,0,'A note from Abercrombie the hermit, eh? I don\'t know him, though if he lives out at the graveyard then I do know his brains have rotted out!',15595),
(252,1,0,'Ah, is the note translated? Please, let me see it...',15595),
(253,1,0,'Have you yet found Eliza\'s grave? Do you have the Embalmer\'s heart?',15595),
(254,1,0,'',15595),
(255,1,0,'Have you had any luck?',15595),
(256,1,0,'Yes? Is there something I can do for you?',15595),
(257,1,0,'No luck? Don\'t feel too bad, $N...$B$BNot everyone can be me.',15595),
(258,1,0,'It\'s only natural to feel sorry for yourself when shown up by someone so new to this world. You shouldn\'t feel bad, $N.$B$BHm? Did I get your name wrong?',15595),
(261,1,0,'The Scourge grows in power with the passing of each day. If you truly wish to halt its advances, then show me.',15595),
(262,1,0,'If you have something that belongs to the shadowy figure for whom you seek, then let me see it. I may be able to divine something of its owner.',15595),
(263,1,0,'Back so soon? In case I didn\'t make myself clear we need you to kill 10 Stonesplinter Shaman and 10 Stonesplinter Bonesnappers, $N. Now go get\'em, Trogg-Slayer!',15595),
(264,1,0,'The stone is cold to the touch, but has obviously been abused. Trash litters the area; nicks and gashes decorate the relief atop the coffin; and the foliage around the grave has started to grow over the site.$b$bNo one cares for whoever is buried here, especially not any victims of the plague.',15595),
(265,1,0,'Sometimes I\'ll sell blank books to scholars and mages, or to anyone who wants to keep a journal.$B$BI remember well everyone to whom I sold a book within the last few months...',15595),
(266,1,0,'The Scarlet Raven doesn\'t see the business it used to, but we still do get travelers passing through.$B$BIf you can describe the person you\'re looking for, maybe I\'ll remember him.',15595),
(267,1,0,'Do you have 8 Trogg Stone Teeth to show me?  If not, there is still work to be done, $N.',15595),
(268,1,0,'Did you find who the Shadowy Figure was?',15595),
(269,1,0,'Rest, $gbrother:sister;. I can tell you have traveled far, and you bear a heavy burden. Can you tell me what casts that dark shadow over you?',15595),
(270,1,0,NULL,15595),
(271,1,0,'Ah, $N! Back so soon? No doubt you\'ve been at the hunt again? Don\'t worry if you\'ve had some setbacks, in the long run it will make you better!$B$B... You couldn\'t get much worse, anyway...',15595),
(273,1,0,NULL,15595),
(274,1,0,'What is that you bring from Ashlan?',15595),
(275,1,0,'The Wetlands still weep, and the Fen Creepers still rage. Return to me when your task is done.',15595),
(276,1,0,'Your task is still at hand, young $C.',15595),
(277,1,0,'Do you have the Gnolls\' tools for fire?',15595),
(278,1,0,'Do you have the needed items? Time is of the essence!!',15595),
(279,1,0,'Our merchants will not be safe until we are rid of Gobbler and those Murlocs.',15595),
(280,1,0,'The top of the keg slowly twists off.',15595),
(281,1,0,NULL,15595),
(283,1,0,NULL,15595),
(284,1,0,NULL,15595),
(285,1,0,NULL,15595),
(286,1,0,'Do you have the statuette?',15595),
(287,1,0,'You can\'t find it? My directions were very clear! We don\'t have much time, you\'ve got to hurry! Don\'t come back until you\'ve found the cave.',15595),
(288,1,0,'Oh, I\'m so very thirsty! Won\'t you buy a drink for this poor, pathetic fool?',15595),
(289,1,0,'In my dreams, I can sometimes hear the doomed moans of my brethren! Please, good sir, free them from the bonds and quiet their cries.',15595),
(290,1,0,'This chest is securely locked.',15595),
(291,1,0,'Hmm... it would seem that my guards are becoming less discriminatory with petitioners. Well, what do you want? Make it quick.',15595),
(292,1,0,'That drunk Fitzsimmons sent you to me? Well, you can tell him I don\'t have any extra ale. He\'s going to have to panhandle someone else!',15595),
(293,1,0,'What is that orb you have? It looks...soiled.',15595),
(294,1,0,'Kill 10 Mottled Raptors and 10 Mottled Screechers, $N. My co-workers did not deserve the fate that was brought upon them. It\'s time to even the score.',15595),
(295,1,21,'I want to make those Mottled Scytheclaws and Mottled Razormaws pay for what they did. Have you killed 10 of each yet?',15595),
(296,6,2,'Is Sarltooth dead? Have you redeemed the memory of the fallen?',15595),
(297,1,0,'Do you have those Idols? We must study them and report our findings to Ironforge!',15595),
(298,1,0,'Oh, a progress report from the site? Very good!',15595),
(299,6,0,'Have you uncovered the four fragments yet, $N?  Ados, Modr, Golm and Neru...',15595),
(301,1,0,'We Stormpikes don\'t like being bothered with trivial matters, $C. I hope you brought news worthy of my valuable attention.',15595),
(302,1,0,NULL,15595),
(303,1,0,'Roggo has been unable to contact the reserve forces. We need offensive pressure on that Dark Iron encampment, $c. Now get back out there and serve your duty to King Magni!',15595),
(304,1,0,'Were you able to locate Balgaras the Foul yet, $C? He has been evading us for quite some time.',15595),
(305,1,0,NULL,15595),
(306,1,0,'Were you able to find Merrin? Did she send word?',15595),
(307,1,0,'Do you have that Miners\' Gear, $N?',15595),
(308,1,0,'Hmph!  There  is all this booze down here, but I have strict orders not to touch it.  If only I could get a taste of some of our Thunder Ale...that would sharpen my wits, no lying!',15595),
(309,1,0,NULL,15595),
(310,1,0,'The date on this barrel shows that it\'ll soon be tapped.',15595),
(311,1,0,'Did you make the switch?',15595),
(312,1,0,'Were you able to get into my meat locker, $N?',15595),
(313,1,0,'Hey, $N.  Been to the Grizzled Den yet?  Those Wendigos can be fierce.',15595),
(314,1,0,'Vagash still terrorizes the herd!  Please help us by killing the wretched beast.',15595),
(315,1,0,'Do you have that shimmerweed?  I almost have a batch of stout ready to brew, and I want to try throwing the weed in with this mixture.',15595),
(317,1,0,'Preparations are going well.  How goes your hunting?',15595),
(318,1,0,NULL,15595),
(319,1,0,'Have you taken care of those wild animals?',15595),
(320,1,0,'Did you get that Evershine?',15595),
(321,1,0,NULL,15595),
(322,1,0,'How might I ply my craft for you, $C?',15595),
(323,1,0,'Battle hard, $Nn. And do not despair, for despair is evil\'s greatest weapon.',15595),
(324,1,0,'Did you find the lightforge iron you need?',15595),
(325,1,0,'Hello, $N. You haven\'t been gone that long, but I see a fire in your eyes I did not see before.',15595),
(328,1,0,'The strongbox is bound in bronze, very sturdy, and very heavy.',15595),
(329,1,0,'Did you discover who knew Thorsen\'s secret? Is there a traitor among us?',15595),
(330,1,0,NULL,15595),
(331,1,0,NULL,15595),
(332,1,0,'Greetings and welcome, $gmaster:madam;.  Have you yet tried one of our fine wines?',15595),
(333,1,0,'You bring word from Mr. Bagley?',15595),
(334,1,0,'Are you here to buy clothes?',15595),
(335,1,0,'Wishock will soon garner enough support to cause us much grief. Were you able to obtain the Tear of Tilloa or Musquash Root yet?',15595),
(336,1,0,'Can you not see that I am busy? My words must be heard! I am very important to the future of this Kingdom!$B$BOh... what have you there? Why it looks like a refreshing drink...',15595),
(337,1,0,'Ooh! What\'s that old book you have there? Can I see it??',15595),
(338,1,0,'Have you assembled the chapters yet, $N?',15595),
(339,6,0,'I don\'t suppose you were able to track down pages 1, 4, 6 and 8?  Those four are all we need to piece Chapter I back together.',15595),
(340,1,0,'We still need pages 10, 11, 14 and 16 to complete Chapter II, $N.',15595),
(341,6,0,'Any luck with pages 18, 20, 21 or 24?  Those are the only ones we need to piece together Chapter III.',15595),
(342,6,0,'We just need three pages to finish off Chapter IV, $N.  Do you have pages 25, 26 or 27 yet?',15595),
(343,1,0,NULL,15595),
(344,1,0,NULL,15595),
(345,1,0,NULL,15595),
(346,1,0,'Were you able to find the book?',15595),
(347,1,0,'Do you have the Rethban Ore?',15595),
(348,0,0,'....mother?$b$b...so cold...$b$b...heading into the Twisting Nether...h-h-h-hold me mother....',15595),
(349,1,0,'Witch Doctor Unbagwa know what Mokk the Savage like.  Yes, yes!$b$bMe speak with spirits and make he come, I do.$b$bBut other Gorilla-beast like spirit talkin\' too.  You protect Witch Doctor Unbagwa and I make he come to you.$b$bWitch Doctor Unbagwa want something first.  You bring a Gorilla Fang and me start spirit talking!',15595),
(350,1,0,NULL,15595),
(351,1,0,'You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken?  The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:$B$B\"Yes, excellent work!  This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs.  Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover.  The beacon will take care of the rest!\"',15595),
(353,1,0,'You come all the way from Stormwind? I hear it\'s getting dicey down there in the human lands, with brigands and orcs running about. A perfect place for a $C to prove his worth!',15595),
(354,1,0,'Do you have the remains of the Agamands? Are those cursed beasts finally destroyed?',15595),
(355,1,0,NULL,15595),
(356,1,0,'Do you have a report of your patrol?',15595),
(357,1,0,'$N, have you acquired the book?',15595),
(358,1,0,'Is your task complete?  Have you destroyed those dog-things and drained them of their ichor?',15595),
(359,1,0,NULL,15595),
(360,1,0,NULL,15595),
(361,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(362,1,0,'Did you find Devlin?',15595),
(365,1,0,'Deathguard Simmer sent word that you were going to provide me with some much needed reagents. Were you able to gather 10 pumpkins yet, $N?',15595),
(366,1,0,'Your masters are fools to send you here, for I will never again be a Scourge slave!',15595),
(367,1,0,'Have you collected 5 vials of darkhound blood yet, $N? Time is fleeting!',15595),
(368,1,0,'$N, were you able to obtain 5 Vile Fin Scales from the Murlocs?',15595),
(369,1,0,'Do you have some venom from a Vicious Night Web Spider yet, $N? It\'s the final component I need in order to test my experiment.',15595),
(370,1,0,'Young $C, you shouldn\'t be wasting your time here in Brill when your people need you fighting for their cause. Now, take up arms and travel to the southwest, to the ruined tower, and slay Captain Perrine along with 3 Scarlet Zealots and 3 Scarlet Missionaries. We shall herd the Scarlet Crusade like cattle to their demise.',15595),
(371,1,0,'I see you have returned but your task is not complete. Perhaps you are at ease with the mere humans interfering with The Dark Lady\'s plan? Or perhaps you can heed the call of duty and slay Captain Vachon and his band of Scarlet Friars!',15595),
(372,1,5,'You have not yet performed your duty, $c.  We cannot expect to carry out The Dark Lady\'s plan with the Scarlet Crusade pestering our soldiers.  Bring about their deaths and perform your duty to Sylvanas!',15595),
(373,1,0,'Yes? Is there something I can help you with?',15595),
(374,1,0,'Have you collected 10 Scarlet Insignia Rings yet, $c?',15595),
(375,1,0,'Do you have five Duskbat Pelts and some Coarse Thread yet, $N?',15595),
(377,1,0,'So long as a molester of the dead like Dextren Ward is permitted to live, justice stands betrayed. Return to me once Lord Ebonlocke\'s sentence of death is carried out on that defiler, Ward. We shall give the families of the dead the closure they deserve and better yet, we will send a clear message to the House of Nobles in Stormwind.',15595),
(378,1,0,'I won\'t let foolish Human bureaucracy interfere with Dwarven matters, $N. Kam Deepfury is a proven conspirator in the Thandol Span attack. King Magni\'s good people lost their lives because of Deepfury\'s deceit. The Humans might be content to let Deepfury rot in The Stockade but I will not sleep soundly at night until Deepfury is slain.',15595),
(379,1,0,'Well, did the nomads \'volunteer\' up those water pouches for you?',15595),
(384,1,0,'I\'m going to need those crag boar ribs and a mug of Rhapsody Malt, $N.',15595),
(385,1,0,'Did I tell you about the time I almost lost my hand to one of the crocs? Nasty bugger it was, teeth like knives. But I was lucky... Jammed the brute\'s jaw shut with my knife. Still have the knife around here somewhere...',15595),
(386,1,0,'Have you been to Stormwind yet, to The Stockade? I fear whatever trickery that has kept Targorr the Dread alive for this long will eventually bring about his freedom. He was sentenced to die, $N, not act as some political pawn on a noble\'s whim.',15595),
(387,1,0,'The Stockade is still overrun! These Defias Rats must be shown that their actions will not be tolerated. Now get back down there and show some force!',15595),
(388,1,0,'I see you are back, $c.  Have you collected 10 Red Wool Bandanas from those Defias Scum in The Stockade yet?',15595),
(389,1,0,NULL,15595),
(391,1,0,'Either you bring me Thredd\'s head, or I\'ll take yours, understand, $N?',15595),
(392,1,0,'Yes, $N? What have you found?',15595),
(393,1,0,'Greetings. Of what service can I be to you, $C?',15595),
(394,1,0,NULL,15595),
(395,1,0,NULL,15595),
(396,1,0,'$N, yes? I was informed by Baros Alexston that you would be coming. I must say, I am most interested in what you have to say.',15595),
(397,1,0,NULL,15595),
(398,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(399,1,0,'$N! Did you have any luck?',15595),
(400,1,0,'Hm?  You look a little young to be a siege engine pilot.  But no matter...do you need something fixed?$B$BWell take a number and get comfortable.  I\'m working on a couple engines right now and won\'t have time for another job for at least a few days.$B$BOr, were you here for something else...?',15595),
(401,1,0,'',15595),
(403,1,0,'',15595),
(404,0,0,'Have you completed the task with which I have charged you?  Do you have those putrid claws?',15595),
(405,1,0,'Greetings. Either you do not know who I am, or your business with me is urgent.$b$bBecause if neither of these were true, then you would not be foolish enough to disturb me...',15595),
(407,5,0,'Stay away, foul and unholy creature!  May the Light protect me!  The Scarlet Crusade shall rid Azeroth of your. . .$b$b. . .oh wait.  Is that food for me?  I am so hungry. . .',15595),
(408,1,0,'Time is not a luxury we have, $N. With each passing hour, the Scourge\'s hold on Tirisfal Glades grows more firm.',15595),
(409,1,0,'I await proof of your allegiance, $c.',15595),
(410,1,0,'This is an old, beaten, bloody table.',15595),
(411,1,0,'Have you returned Gunther\'s book? Has he responded?',15595),
(412,1,0,'Those pilots can\'t wait to get back into their steam tanks and take to the field again. Let\'s not let them down.',15595),
(413,1,0,'Hello, $C!  And what business takes you all the way out here?$B$BSomething exciting, I hope.  I haven\'t been in a good fight in days, and this barrel of ale is almost dry...',15595),
(414,1,0,'Greetings, $C, and welcome to Thelsamar!',15595),
(415,1,0,NULL,15595),
(416,1,0,'Hail, $N. How goes the rat catching?',15595),
(417,1,0,'Hello, $N. Do you have word of my friend Hildelve?',15595),
(418,1,0,'I\'m all ready to start cooking, do you have the ingredients for me?',15595),
(419,1,0,NULL,15595),
(421,1,1,'If you wish to prove yourself to me, you must kill 5 Moonrage Whitescalps.  Accomplish that task, and I will see to it your skill is put to more worthy assignments.',15595),
(422,1,0,'Before I know what we are dealing with here, $C, I need to study the spell known as Remedy of Arugal. Bring it to me now or I shall be forced to find myself a worthy servant.',15595),
(423,1,0,'I will need 6 Glutton Shackles and 3 Darksoul Shackles before I can assess the situation and devise a final solution for Arugal. Now heed your bidding and slay Moonrage Gluttons and Moonrage Darksouls until you have what I need.',15595),
(424,1,0,'Has Grimson the Pale been slain? Varimathras will not be pleased if we ignore his bidding.',15595),
(425,1,0,'Have you killed Ivar the Foul? If you won\'t do it for me and my brother, then do it for the Forsaken.',15595),
(426,1,0,'Our battles with the Scourge wage on, $N. Do your part and throw those cursed, mindless undead back into the Plaguelands!',15595),
(427,1,0,'If you wish to prove your worth to The Dark Lady, slay 10 Scarlet Warriors, $C.',15595),
(428,1,0,NULL,15595),
(429,0,0,'My time is short, $c, for the Dark Lady has charged me with a grave task.',15595),
(430,1,0,'My sister told me you were here to aid us. Is that true?',15595),
(431,1,0,NULL,15595),
(432,1,0,'It makes me so mad! Grrr...',15595),
(433,1,0,'If we can remove the troggs from Gol\'Bolar quarry, it will be the first step of many that we will have to undertake to rid ourselves of this menace.',15595),
(434,1,0,'Yes, $N? Are things going well with Tyrion? He apprised me of the situation and I\'ve helped him trick Marzon into going to the castle.$B$BMarzon has been a thorn in the side of many people in Stormwind; many of which are close friends of mine. No one messes with my friends... not if they know what\'s healthy for them.$B$BIt\'s just a shame I\'m indirectly doing a favor for Shaw and SI:7 in the meantime. Oh well, not every plan is perfect.',15595),
(435,1,0,NULL,15595),
(436,1,0,NULL,15595),
(437,1,0,'Have you defeated Nightlash, $N?  Our success against the rot hides depends on her destruction!',15595),
(438,1,0,NULL,15595),
(439,1,0,'$N. You return, so I assume your investigations bore fruit?',15595),
(440,1,0,'Hello, $N. What brings you back to Brill?',15595),
(441,1,0,'Do I know you?',15595),
(442,1,0,'The Scourge cannot be allowed to remain in Silverpine, $N. Come back to me when you have proof of Thule\'s death.',15595),
(443,1,0,'Do you have the rot hide ichor, $N?',15595),
(444,1,0,'My studies require great concentration. So I hope your visit is not a frivolous one.',15595),
(445,1,0,'What business do you have with me, $C?',15595),
(446,1,0,'Greetings, $N. What did Bethor have to say?',15595),
(447,1,0,'Hail, $C. What business do you have with the Royal Apothecary Society?',15595),
(448,1,0,NULL,15595),
(449,1,0,'Did you discover the fate of the Deathstalkers?',15595),
(450,1,0,'I see you are back, $N.',15595),
(451,1,0,'What brings you back to the Undercity, $N?',15595),
(452,1,0,NULL,15595),
(453,1,0,'Who are you?? Leave me be!',15595),
(454,1,0,NULL,15595),
(455,1,0,'You\'re coming from Loch Modan? How is the orc situation at Algaz Gate?',15595),
(460,1,0,'This grave was hastily dug.',15595),
(461,1,0,'This is the spot! Bring me closer...',15595),
(463,1,0,NULL,15595),
(464,1,0,'Have you attacked the Dragonmaw encampment?',15595),
(465,1,0,'The first catapult is before you. Will you set it aflame?',15595),
(466,1,0,'Where is that ore, $N?!',15595),
(467,1,0,NULL,15595),
(468,1,0,NULL,15595),
(469,1,0,'Hello there, $C. Could I interest you in a pair of boots? Perhaps some newly cured skins?',15595),
(470,1,0,'Did you find my bag?',15595),
(471,18,11,'My apprentice is like a son to me. It\'s going to be hard for him to live his life with only one leg.$b$bAh, $N, how goes it? Do you have my skins?',15595),
(472,1,0,NULL,15595),
(473,1,0,NULL,15595),
(474,1,0,'Have you killed Nek\'rosh?',15595),
(476,0,5,NULL,15595),
(477,1,0,NULL,15595),
(478,1,0,'Have you learned anything useful, $N?',15595),
(479,1,0,'We must hurry, their plans must not come to fruition, or we may lose our hold on Silverpine Forest.',15595),
(480,1,0,'Quickly, time runs short, $N!',15595),
(481,1,0,'Yes, $C? What is it?',15595),
(482,1,0,NULL,15595),
(483,1,0,'$N, the kidnapped Druids of the Talon will be forever trapped in the Emerald Dream if we cannot retrieve the Relics of Wakening from the Ban\'ethil Barrow Den to the west.$b$bFor every minute we delay their fate comes one step closer to eternal doom.',15595),
(484,1,0,'$N, right? Do you have my skins?',15595),
(485,1,0,'You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken?  The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:\n\n\"Yes, excellent work!  This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs.  Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover - the beacon will take care of the rest!\"',15595),
(486,1,0,'Our brethren cannot be awakened until Ursal the Mauler has been slain, $N.',15595),
(487,1,0,'The road is still not safe, $c. Travel forth and slay 6 Gnarlpine Ambushers and return to me.',15595),
(488,0,0,'Have you been a busy little bee, $N?  I\'ve been waiting for you to bring me what I need.',15595),
(489,4,0,'What do you have for me, $N?  A lovely snack I presume?',15595),
(491,1,0,'$N. Have you defeated Thule Ravenclaw?',15595),
(492,14,0,'Why if I had my trusted rifle you\'d be as good as dead, $C.  Just wait until the Steam Tank Brigade arrives to rescue me!',15595),
(493,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(494,1,0,NULL,15595),
(495,1,0,NULL,15595),
(496,1,0,'I see you are back. I hope you were able to gather the agents I need. Another deathless day will put me in such a gloomy mood.',15595),
(498,1,0,'You must make haste, $C. I shudder to think what the humans might be doing to Drull and Tog\'thar.',15595),
(499,1,0,'Ribbit!',15595),
(501,1,0,'I remember you, $N. You were going to help me out in concocting my latest elixir. I\'ll need that blood before I can bring my own special brand of misery to the inhabitants of Hillsbrad.',15595),
(502,1,0,'Woof?',15595),
(503,1,0,'Give me the key, $C, I will undo the lock myself.',15595),
(506,1,0,NULL,15595),
(507,1,0,'W-what do you want?',15595),
(508,1,0,'You\'ve returned, $N. Success to report?',15595),
(509,1,0,'Any luck at Nethander Stead?',15595),
(513,1,0,'Can you not see I am busy, $C? The Dark Lady insists on a new plague before the Scourge advance from Northrend overwhelms us. And with the human threat pressing from the south, time becomes my most precious commodity. This better be important!',15595),
(515,1,0,'So glad to see you back, $N. I was growing so terribly bored here. Not a single entertaining thing to do besides poison and disease Umpi and reanimate her. . .over and over and over again.$b$bHow went the trip to the Undercity? Were you fortunate enough to slaughter any humans along the way?',15595),
(516,1,0,'Have you located their base yet, $n? Time is of the essence!',15595),
(517,1,0,'Sometimes I get so bored out here in Tarren Mill I like to open up the formaldehyde jar and let the lovely aroma waft through the air. Makes Umpi a little nervous though.$b$bSo were you able to get a keg from the Dwarves? I swear if I have to stare at this deadly elixir without using on it someone for another day I am going to scream.',15595),
(518,1,0,'I note that your task is unfinished, $N. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?',15595),
(519,1,0,'I want their heads, $N, not excuses.',15595),
(520,1,0,'Three heads I have, a fourth I need. It will be Mug\'Thol\'s, or it will be yours, $N. That I promise.',15595),
(521,1,0,'Yes? Do you have something to report?',15595),
(524,1,0,'A musty smell emanates from the rug.',15595),
(526,1,0,'Did you find the lightforge iron you need?',15595),
(527,1,0,'As High Executor of Tarren Mill, under the direct command of Varimathras and the Dark Lady, you are subject to follow my command.$B$BPerhaps you take this war with the Alliance lightly? If such is the case I should behead you right here and now. Otherwise, travel west to the town of Hillsbrad and wage battle against the humans, as ordered.$B$BDismissed.',15595),
(528,1,0,'You have your orders, $c. Quit dawdling here in Tarren Mill when there is work to be done elsewhere.',15595),
(529,1,0,'Were you able to carry out your orders, $C? Did you dispose of Verringtan and his assistants? And where is that iron shipment?',15595),
(530,1,0,'Do you have those hands, $N?',15595),
(531,1,0,'Great job, $N! We really showed him! Here, give me the head and I\'ll take care of it.',15595),
(532,1,0,'What news have you?',15595),
(533,1,0,'Have you found anything? I fear Gol\'dir\'s prospects grow worse by the day...',15595),
(536,1,0,'Another ale, please, the last one just seemed to have disappeared!$B$BLight, how much longer am I going to be stuck out here?$B$BOh, it\'s you, $N. Have you killed those murlocs yet?',15595),
(538,1,0,NULL,15595),
(539,1,0,'You were given direct orders to attack the Azureload Mine. Your reasons for loafing about Tarren Mill better be good or I will behead you for treason.',15595),
(540,1,0,'I wish I could search the ruins too, but I fear these bones wouldn\'t hold me during my climb up the mountains. However, how does your hunt for knowledge progress, $N?',15595),
(541,1,0,'Dun Garok proves to be too much of an obstacle for you, $C? And here I thought you had established yourself valiantly in Hillsbrad.$B$BIf you\'re not up to handle the mission assigned to you, I will find another who can produce better results. As for you, well, I am sure the Dark Lady could always use more grave diggers back in Tirisfal Glades.',15595),
(542,1,0,'$N, you\'ve returned! How did your foray into Alterac go? Did you bring anything back with you?',15595),
(543,1,0,'Salutations, $N. Do try to avoid stepping on my pant cuffs. This outfit is newly tailored.',15595),
(544,0,0,'Did you find the thieves?  And more importantly, did you find what they stole?',15595),
(545,1,0,'Have you yet thinned the Dalaran patrols around their ruins?',15595),
(546,1,0,'So the lucky $N returns? How many humans have you slaughtered today? Hundreds I do hope!$b$bHave you any skulls for me?',15595),
(547,1,0,'Were you able to retrieve my sword, $N? High Executor Darthalia will hang me from the rafters if she discovers my folly.',15595),
(549,1,0,'Do you have nothing better to do than stand here before me, $c? As High Executor, I have more pressing matters than to stare at your rotting visage.',15595),
(550,1,0,'What brings a $C all the way to the Undercity from the battlefield?',15595),
(552,1,0,'Have you recovered Helcular\'s Rod yet? There are so many Yeti in this region, it will be very difficult to locate. But we must have it in order to proceed.',15595),
(553,1,0,'Helcular\'s grave teems with a mystical energy.',15595),
(555,1,0,'Any luck finding the ingredients? I\'ll tell you, this territory isn\'t the peaceful place it once was. Ah, if only this unrest never occurred...',15595),
(556,0,0,'Do you have the Worn Stone Tokens, $N?  The Magus is eager to unlock their secrets.',15595),
(557,1,0,'Hello, $N. Elementals are tough quarry, but I know you\'re up to the task. Do you have those bracers of binding?',15595),
(559,1,0,'Did you get those heads for me, $N?',15595),
(560,1,0,'Greetings, citizen. Have you come to lend your arm to upholding the safety of Southshore?',15595),
(561,1,0,NULL,15595),
(562,1,0,'I\'ve a letter ready to go to Major Samuelson in Stormwind. All I need are the results.',15595),
(563,1,0,'Greetings, citizen. May the Stormwind city guard be of assistance?',15595),
(564,1,0,'Mountain Lions killin\' off our horses left and right and here you are wantin\' to jibber-jabber about the weather and what not.$B$BOught to go and find myself a real hero. More killin\' and less talkin\'.',15595),
(565,1,0,'So you have returned to the great Bartolo. Perhaps you have finished gathering the materials needed for your Yeti Fur Cloak? Or maybe you just enjoy basking in the greatness of me, Bartolo!',15595),
(566,1,0,'Ah, $N. Perhaps you\'ve come to collect the bounty on the head of Baron Vardus?',15595),
(567,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(568,1,0,'Our supply efforts are still being hampered by the indigenous raptor population, $c.',15595),
(569,1,0,'Have you made any progress with the ogres of the Mizjah Ruins yet, $C?',15595),
(570,1,0,'What news do you bring?',15595),
(571,1,0,'Has fortune been on your side, $N? Were you able to obtain an aged gorilla sinew?',15595),
(572,1,0,'Did your gathering efforts prove fruitful?',15595),
(573,1,0,'I am almost ready to complete the enchantment. Have you performed my bidding?',15595),
(574,1,0,'Sergeant Yohwa tells me you are skilled and brave, $C. Do you have something to report?',15595),
(575,0,0,'My equipment is all ready to go, $n, I just need those skins. We don\'t want to keep Riddlevox waiting, that\'s for sure.$b$bIt\'s not a good idea for anyone to keep the chief inventor of the Tinkers\' Union unsatisfied.',15595),
(576,1,0,'Ahoy, me bucko!  Might not be able to see but I can smell ye from halfway across port.$b$bCould really use me eye back.  Captain\'s going to keelhaul me when he finds out me peeper is in the hands of them dirty Bloodsail Buccaneers.$b$bWhat good is a lookout who can\'t see?  The crow\'s nest used to be me home...without me deadlights I\'d be lucky to scrub the bilge.',15595),
(577,1,0,'Drizzlik\'s Excelsior leather boots, finest workmanship, one-hundred percent high quality saltwater crocilisk skin boots. None finer!$b$bCan\'t beat a glowing description like that, can you?$b$bExcept, maybe, if you have those skins for me?',15595),
(578,1,0,'The trolls truly possessed some amazing magical objects, $N. And now, perhaps, I have the opportunity to add one to my extensive collection. Did you have any luck finding the source of the rumor?',15595),
(579,1,0,'King Varian has placed great importance on learning, and thus has provided funds for making copies of various tomes and writings available to the public. It\'s very simple. You bring me a library scrip, and I can give you a copy of one of the available books.',15595),
(580,5,0,'Sink me!  I\'m almost outta booze here!  Cap\'n is goin\' to weigh anchor and Ol\' Slim will be caught dry as the Tanaris Desert.  And once he discovers his port is missing. . . blimey!',15595),
(581,1,0,'$C. Show me you have made prey of the Bloodscalp tribe.$b$bShow me your trophies.',15595),
(582,1,0,'$N. I fear for our chief\'s son. Do you have the shrunken heads so I may inspect them?',15595),
(583,1,0,NULL,15595),
(584,1,0,'The greenish broth within the cauldron bubbles.',15595),
(585,0,0,'I await the skulls...',15595),
(586,1,0,'Although my own flesh boils off my skull, I can still smell your fear.$B$BHah!  You will never complete my task...',15595),
(587,1,0,'Any luck finding the goods, matey?',15595),
(588,1,0,NULL,15595),
(589,1,0,'Do you have the shards, $N? They are needed for my final ritual, after we have the Mind\'s Eye.',15595),
(591,1,0,'Greetings, $N. The spirits sing praise of your bravery, yet they tell me no tales of your quest against Mai\'Zoth.$b$bDo you have the Eye?',15595),
(592,1,0,'$N. Kin\'weelay told me you set out to capture Yenniku.$b$bIs it true? Do you have him?',15595),
(593,1,0,'Yenniku stands stunned before you, his mind in another place...',15595),
(594,1,0,NULL,15595),
(595,1,0,NULL,15595),
(596,1,0,'The Bloodscalps will one day be crushed by the Darkspears! Do you have the necklaces of our doomed foe?',15595),
(597,1,0,NULL,15595),
(598,1,0,'The Skullsplitters will curse the day they brought us to war! Is your task complete?',15595),
(599,1,0,NULL,15595),
(600,1,0,'Do you have those crystals?? I need them!!$b$bI mean...I need to know the evil Venture Company is losing ground in Stranglethorn. Because, you know, we honest folk have to make a living!',15595),
(601,1,0,'Have you had any luck, $N?',15595),
(602,1,0,'If you wouldn\'t mind, I am rather busy right now.',15595),
(603,1,0,NULL,15595),
(604,1,0,'Ahoy, $n.  What word do you bring of the Bloodsail encampment to the south?',15595),
(605,0,0,'Do you have those shards yet?  I\'ll give you a decent cut from the profits!',15595),
(606,1,0,'Hey!  I don\'t like the look you\'re giving me, $gmister:lady;.',15595),
(607,1,0,'Here here, $N.  Did you get Shaky\'s payment?',15595),
(608,1,0,'What\'s the problem, $N? We need to attack before the Bloodsail Buccaneers do!',15595),
(609,0,0,'$N, did you find those three dogs? Did you collect their valuables?',15595),
(610,1,0,'I\'d never been beat before, you know, $N? Sure I\'d been cut, can\'t get in a knife fight without that, but he just smacked me on the side of the head, blacked me out. When I came to my blade was gone.$B$BAs much as my nickname might indicate, I still need a knife to fight, and for me, it has to be that one.',15595),
(611,1,0,'Have you retrieved the Stone of the Tides for me, $N? I\'ve already cleared out a space and purchased a fine stand for it.',15595),
(613,1,0,'Ahoy, $N! Have you yet found Maury\'s Key?',15595),
(614,1,0,'Ahoy, $N! Did you find Gorlash? That chest was my favorite, and it has a hidden compartment that held my greatest treasures!',15595),
(615,1,0,NULL,15595),
(616,1,0,NULL,15595),
(617,1,0,'If ya got no business with me, then move along, $N.',15595),
(618,1,0,'Did you get my cutlass, $N?',15595),
(619,1,0,'This is an abandoned lifeboat.  Printed along its side in scratched, faded paint are the words:$B$B\"Smotts\' Revenge\"',15595),
(620,1,0,NULL,15595),
(621,0,0,'Do you have the samples of Zanzil\'s Mixture??',15595),
(622,1,0,'Hello, $N. Did you make it to Booty Bay? Did the goblin Krazek fix my pot??',15595),
(623,1,0,'Yeah?',15595),
(624,1,0,'',15595),
(625,1,0,'',15595),
(626,1,0,'',15595),
(627,1,0,'Hello, $N. Did you have luck getting the bloodstone?',15595),
(628,1,0,'I read somewhere that the saltwater crocilisks are slowly dying out... bad news for my business, isn\'t it?$b$bAnyways, I hope you have that elder saltwater crocolisk skin for me!',15595),
(629,1,0,'I await the Tablet Shard, $N.',15595),
(630,1,0,'I thank my ancestors someone has come to aid me. Do you have the key that will free me?',15595),
(631,1,0,NULL,15595),
(632,1,0,'Any sign of Ol\' Rustlocke, $N?',15595),
(633,1,0,'The cache of explosives must be destroyed!',15595),
(634,1,0,NULL,15595),
(635,1,0,NULL,15595),
(636,1,0,NULL,15595),
(637,1,0,'You look as though you have traveled a great distance and seen much turmoil in your time, $C. These times we live in are trying on the soul. What news do you bring to me now?',15595),
(638,1,0,NULL,15595),
(639,1,0,'Have you located the first sigil yet? It is most likely carried on the person of one of the Syndicate agents in Stromgarde.',15595),
(640,0,0,'Throm\'ka, $c. Zengu informed me that you required my assistance?',15595),
(641,1,0,'$N! Do you have the second sigil?',15595),
(642,0,0,'This cluster of shards looks much like the Shards of Myzrael.  But the same feeling of security does not pulse through them.',15595),
(643,1,0,'Valorcall will not be easy to track down, $N. Mounted on horseback, he can cover ground quickly. Nonetheless, we must have his sigil.',15595),
(644,1,0,'You\'ve returned, $N. Is the line of Ignaeus Trollbane broken?',15595),
(645,1,0,'Etchings in the stone upon the face of the tomb of Trollbane match the glowing lines of the Sigil of Ignaeus...',15595),
(646,1,0,'$N! Have you taken the sword?',15595),
(647,1,0,'What\'s the good word, $R?',15595),
(648,1,0,NULL,15595),
(649,1,0,NULL,15595),
(650,1,0,NULL,15595),
(651,1,0,'This is the Stone of Inner Binding. It is the strongest of the binding stones and must be unlocked for the others to open.',15595),
(652,1,0,'The Keystone is charged with tremendous geomantic energy.',15595),
(653,1,0,NULL,15595),
(654,1,5,'Well, did you get everything you needed? If you didn\'t and the power runs out, everything inside will be ruined and you\'ll have to start over.$B$BHey, don\'t look to me for sympathy; I\'m all about the Gadgetzan Water Company making a profit, and if that means selling you power sources until we can afford to import water in from the icy springs of Dun Morogh, so be it!',15595),
(655,1,0,NULL,15595),
(656,1,0,'The Shards of Myzrael are now strangely quiet.',15595),
(657,1,0,NULL,15595),
(658,1,0,'We appreciate your help in looking for that courier, $N.$B$BWhile you were gone, Kin saw an apothecary come out of that same house to the south of here. I\'m confident that they\'re up to no good--I just need proof of it before we go off and do something rash.$B$BHave you had any luck yet?',15595),
(659,1,0,NULL,15595),
(660,1,0,NULL,15595),
(661,1,0,NULL,15595),
(662,0,0,'How goes the search and recovery mission, $n?  We really need to get those Logs and Charts back from the Maiden\'s Folly and Spirit of Silverpine.$b$bIf the information from those sources were to fall into enemy hands, Fleet Master Seahorn would force us down the plank.$b$bThat is if we ever get out of this mess...',15595),
(663,1,0,NULL,15595),
(664,1,0,'Bah, maybe I should go kill those naga scum myself. It\'s obvious you\'re not goin\' to do it.$B$BMaybe I can find some knitting needles so you can keep yourself busy.',15595),
(665,1,0,'This is no time to talk! The goggles need to be charged with the power of the stone!',15595),
(666,1,0,'How did the goggles work? Did everything function properly? Adjustments can be made if necessary.$b$bOh, and I\'ll need those goggles back when you\'re done. I am sure Captain O\'Breen will have many uses for them later on.',15595),
(667,1,0,NULL,15595),
(668,1,0,'Ahoy, $C. What brings you to the bridge?',15595),
(669,1,0,'What brings you to Booty Bay, $C?',15595),
(670,1,0,'So was Seahorn impressed? I bet you his smile reached from Booty Bay to Ratchet.',15595),
(671,1,0,'Once-cursed blood still runs through my veins, $N. If someone... something is summoning demons, it must be stopped.',15595),
(672,1,0,'I will create an amulet that will give Gor\'mul some of the strength of the raptors. Perhaps that will awaken some flame within him...',15595),
(673,1,0,'The burning in my blood... it grows by the day. The $C must be stopped.',15595),
(674,1,0,'What hope is there when the hand of a coward can slay the mightiest of the mightiest? What hope, I ask you!',15595),
(675,1,0,NULL,15595),
(676,1,0,'I have not the time to sharpen my axe, let alone leave the outpost to slay those beasts that would try and slay my kin.$B$BYou do not seem to have the experience of a grunt let alone a full-fledged warrior, what do you want, $N?',15595),
(677,1,0,'If you have not yet completed my task, then perhaps you are a coward in heart as well as a tyro in war.',15595),
(678,1,0,'You hesitate. Why? You have shown great strength thus far, $N. Do not fail me now.',15595),
(679,1,0,'I see your courage finally wanes. It seems my instincts were correct about you: your strength is nothing compared to your bravado.$b$bReturn to me when the beast\'s head has been severed, or return never again.',15595),
(680,1,0,'Near the Tower of Arathor--that is where you will find Or\'Kalar. His death will stop the attacks on Hammerfall and protect my husband\'s life.$B$BI see in your eyes that you think me weak--even dishonorable--for my silence. Some day you will learn what it is to love as I do. Perhaps then you will understand a different kind of strength and honor.$B$BIn the meantime, do as I ask, and slay Or\'Kalar.',15595),
(681,1,0,'$N, with each passing hour our hold on Stromgarde grows more tenuous. You must make haste or our city will surely fall.',15595),
(682,1,0,'Have you retrieved any Stromgarde Badges, $N? The Syndicate must learn they cannot profit from our dead.',15595),
(683,1,0,'So you are $N the $C? News of your contributions to the Alliance has traveled quite far, you know?$B$BOn what business do you come before me today?',15595),
(684,1,0,'Greetings, $C. You have a report to make?',15595),
(685,1,0,'Hello. Do you have a report to submit?',15595),
(686,1,0,NULL,15595),
(687,1,0,NULL,15595),
(688,1,0,NULL,15595),
(689,1,0,'$N, $N, $N! Tell me you have enough Alterac Granite for me to begin my masterpiece in honor of Sully Balloo.',15595),
(690,1,0,NULL,15595),
(691,1,0,'Have you had any luck so far, $N?$B$B<Kryten makes some notes in his journal as he reads.>$B$BIf my research is correct, the tusks should come from any Witherbark troll. The medicine pouches come from the Witherbark witch doctors, and the strongest of the Witherbark shadow hunters should carry the special knife given to them after they\'ve completed their rites of passage. There\'s no way to tell which shadow hunters will have the knife until you do battle.',15595),
(692,1,0,'Did you find those fragments?!?! You\'ll need the Scroll of Myzrael if you want to trap her again, before it\'s too late!',15595),
(693,1,0,'Our goal is the wand, $N. Focus on that for now.',15595),
(694,1,0,'$N, hello again. Have you found an azure agate yet?',15595),
(695,1,0,NULL,15595),
(696,1,0,'You do this, an\' I\'m sure Malin\'ll be more than pleased with you.',15595),
(697,1,0,'Yes? You look vaguely familiar. I do apologize, but have we met? I get so busy I lose track.',15595),
(698,1,0,'Lok\'tar, $C. Traveling through the swamps isn\'t a risk taken lightly. You\'re brave to test your mettle here.',15595),
(699,1,0,'Good mead, a warm fire, an army of orcs and an arsenal of weapons... that\'s all we really need out here along the coast. I don\'t regret my position out here safeguarding Stonard, but it would be nice if we could one day get a burrow, or at least a tower.',15595),
(700,1,0,NULL,15595),
(701,1,0,'My preparations are made, all I require are the raptor hearts.',15595),
(702,1,0,'Returned again have you? Indeed there is nothing more I could wish for now than more of Tor\'gan\'s pity.$B$BWhat have you for me this time? Perhaps a piece of brightly colored string? Or a length of rope to end this misery of mine...',15595),
(703,1,0,'Hello, $N. Did you bring me my wings?',15595),
(705,1,0,'Did you get my pearls?  I\'m almost out of flash bombs!',15595),
(706,1,0,'How goes the hunt, $C?',15595),
(707,1,0,NULL,15595),
(708,1,0,NULL,15595),
(710,6,0,'This area\'s perfect for-- Could you hold these in place for a moment? Yes, just like that, along the vector normal. Now, what was I... Right. Perfect for testing my latest project. The raw materials, the open space... what more could an intelligent and enlightened practitioner of the arts ask for?',15595),
(711,0,0,'I\'m most pleased, $N. My spells affected the smaller pieces just as I predicted. If this experiment is as successful as I foresee, then the elementals I\'ll be able to control will put anything summoned prior to this to shame.',15595),
(712,1,0,'The stone slabs you found were ideal, $N. Lucien will be taking the extra ones back to Kharanos when we\'re done here. After all, they could prove useful again.$B$BFor instance, they\'d be a nice basis for a handy little shelter once I start looking into a multidisciplinary approach to high-yield explosives...',15595),
(713,6,0,'Have you found the oil I need? It would be so helpful if you were able to find some.',15595),
(714,1,0,'Yes, yes, yes. Just a moment.$b$b',15595),
(715,1,0,'He\'s getting closer to finishing. How are things going on your end?',15595),
(716,1,0,'I wouldn\'t wait too long to get that bracer, Orthanc.$b$bWho knows what\'s going to happen next?',15595),
(717,1,0,'Strong magics and powers held the drakes\' prison for so long, but we cannot allow any possibility that Blacklash and Hematus may be released.',15595),
(718,1,0,'The desert\'s a bad place to be hungry, my friend, let me tell you that.$B$BHey... what\'s that over there...',15595),
(719,1,0,'Not sure what the Shadowforge were lookin\' for, but they definitely had a purpose.',15595),
(720,1,0,NULL,15595),
(723,1,0,'I\'d say it was a bad day, but this is the Badlands: every day\'s a bad day.',15595),
(724,1,0,'Ah, yes. Another traveler seeking something from the dwarves.$B$BMa\'am, I\'m truly sorry, but I\'ve no time to answer meaningless questions right now.',15595),
(725,1,0,'Hmm? Yes, $C.',15595),
(726,1,0,NULL,15595),
(727,1,0,'Hello. Welcome to my shop, but watch what you touch.$B$BKnowledge can be deadly.',15595),
(728,1,0,'Ah, we have an eager $C, I see. Are you here to learn from my collection? Good!$B$BBut be warned: just as knowledge gives power to the strong...it will drive the weak mad.',15595),
(729,1,0,'',15595),
(730,1,0,'',15595),
(731,1,0,'Is the prospector alive?',15595),
(732,1,0,'The nomadic band of ogres travels between their camps across the Badlands; heat rising from the dry earth and the swirling winds will make it difficult to track their progress. I have heard that sometimes they travel through Camp Boff. If you are lost, you might try your search there.',15595),
(733,1,0,'Well, I\'ve made do with what I could, but... it\'s not much. Have you found any more supplies?',15595),
(734,1,0,NULL,15595),
(735,1,0,'Do you have the relics for which I asked?',15595),
(736,0,0,'How goes your mission, $c.',15595),
(737,1,0,'Ho! You were gone a long time. Did you get the digest?',15595),
(738,1,0,NULL,15595),
(739,1,0,'Do you have news of Agmond\'s fate? Did you find him?',15595),
(741,1,0,'What can I do for you, $R?',15595),
(742,1,0,NULL,15595),
(743,1,0,'The Windfuries are deadly foes. Their strength in battle is only rivaled by their desire for fresh meat.',15595),
(744,0,0,'This headdress will certainly be a wonderful gift for my brother.',15595),
(745,1,0,'If the Palemanes had respected the land and its inhabitants more, this conflict would have never occurred.',15595),
(746,0,0,'Hello, $N.  Do you have the Broken Tools?  The dwarves\' digging will enrage the kodos of Mulgore.  This defilement must be stopped!',15595),
(748,1,0,'Do you have the paws and talons, $N?',15595),
(749,1,0,'',15595),
(751,1,0,'Hail, $N. Have you learned anything new about the Venture Co.\'s plans and operations in our homeland?\n\nIf they plan to exploit our lands as they have others, the Outrunners will be quick to put an end to it.',15595),
(754,1,0,NULL,15595),
(756,1,0,'$N, do you have the claws I sent you to gather? The Thunderhorn Water Well grows more tainted with each passing hour!',15595),
(758,1,0,NULL,15595),
(759,1,0,'$N. Do you have the teeth I asked for?',15595),
(760,1,0,NULL,15595),
(761,0,0,'Have you found the swoops, $N.  Do you have their quills?',15595),
(762,1,0,'Time is of the essence, $N. Ragnaros will not wait for us to prepare.',15595),
(764,1,0,'',15595),
(765,1,0,'I seethe with anger at the thought of the atrocities the Venture Co. is willing to perpetrate against us in the name of profit.',15595),
(766,1,0,'My fever grows worse and I find my mind drifting into delirious nightmares... I should have known that I wouldn\'t be able to handle a beast my grandfather was unable to defeat...$b$bDo you have the ingredients for the remedy? I fear if I do not clean the infection soon, it will be the death of me.',15595),
(767,1,0,NULL,15595),
(768,1,0,'Hello again. Have you been hunting? Do you have skins for me?',15595),
(769,1,0,'Do you have my supplies, $N?',15595),
(770,1,0,'',15595),
(771,1,0,'Once you have gathered enough well stones from around the water wells and Ambercorn from beneath the trees, I will prepare the Water of the Seers for you.',15595),
(772,1,0,NULL,15595),
(773,1,0,NULL,15595),
(775,1,0,NULL,15595),
(776,1,0,'Have you tracked down Arra\'chea yet?',15595),
(777,1,0,'<Without looking up from the shackles, Lotwil holds out a hand and waggles his fingers impatiently.>$B$BThe cog, $N, the cog!',15595),
(778,1,0,'Not quite the outcome I was expecting. Could you get my shackles back?',15595),
(779,1,0,'The Seal of the Earth lies here, with three recessed alcoves for the Amethyst Runestone, the Opal Runestone, and the Diamond Runestone.',15595),
(782,1,0,'Tho\'grun\'s betrayal... is there any wonder why the ogres are part of the Horde no longer? I will be glad to see him dead, and the Sign of the Earth returned.$B$BIf you\'ve not dispatched him yet, then waste no time going to Camp Boff.  It is to the southeast of Kargath.',15595),
(784,1,0,'You have your orders, $N. The safety of Durotar is in question. Complete the task before you or hang your head in shame.$B$BShow your honor and defeat the humans of Tiragarde Keep.',15595),
(786,1,5,'The centaurs have proven to be a consistent nuisance to the Horde. Their intentions to lay siege to our homeland cannot be tolerated.',15595),
(791,1,0,'I fought proudly alongside the Warchief when these lands were pioneered. The scars of battle mark my skin.$b$bThe honor of the Horde has been upheld with the help of my axe and battlecry during the defeat of Archimonde, when the unholy alliance was made with the humans and elves, wrought from necessity.$b$bBut my position as watchman and provider has given me a new sense of worth.',15595),
(793,0,0,'There are few enemies more deadly than dragonkind, and there were few dragons that fought as ferociously as Blacklash and Hematus.',15595),
(795,1,0,'The Seal of the Earth lies here, with three recessed alcoves for the Amethyst Runestone, the Opal Runestone, and the Diamond Runestone.',15595),
(806,1,0,'Did you find Fizzle, $N? He, and rest of the Burning Blade, must be scoured from our lands!',15595),
(808,1,0,'Do you have my brother\'s skull, $N? Is he finally free?',15595),
(809,1,0,NULL,15595),
(812,1,0,'I\'m almost glad I can\'t return to Sen\'jin as I am now. My weakness and stupidity would surely be mocked.',15595),
(813,1,0,'Remember, no matter what creature you hunt, you would do well to study it and understand its behavior. That knowledge could save your life.',15595),
(815,1,0,'Breakfast, lunch, dinner! Who cares which meal it is? It still has to be cooked by someone--namely me!',15595),
(816,1,0,'I pray that Kron will return to me, but I\'m almost certain I know his fate already.',15595),
(817,1,0,'I remember my first tiger hunt, $N. I chose to hunt on the largest of the Echo Isles, and I sat perfectly still in the shadows of its foliage for almost a full day... watching... waiting.$b$bMy muscles were taut, and I was ready to strike. It was one of my greatest victories when that tiger finally took the bait.',15595),
(818,1,0,'Time is the true test of your strength and will. Lose patience or give in to weakness, and your true self will be shown.',15595),
(819,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(821,1,0,'How\'s the search going?',15595),
(822,1,0,'You working hard at finding those ingredients, $N?',15595),
(823,1,0,NULL,15595),
(824,1,0,'Ah, hello there. I spend a great deal of time studying the water - all the elements really - so much so that sometimes I don\'t even notice people around me.$b$bIs there something I can help you with?',15595),
(825,1,0,'Once we learn how the humans operate their strange machinery, we will stand a greater chance of defeating them in future battles.$b$bWith our new gained knowledge, the Horde only stands to grow in strength.',15595),
(826,1,0,'Is Zalazane defeated, $N?',15595),
(827,1,0,'Have you yet entered Skull Rock, $N? Do you have the Searing Collars?',15595),
(828,1,0,NULL,15595),
(829,1,0,'My most humble greetings, $C. How might I help my $R brother today?',15595),
(830,1,0,'There is a look of concern on your face, $C. What have you there?',15595),
(831,1,0,'Can you not see that I am busy? This had better be pressing....',15595),
(832,1,0,'You have something vital to report. I can sense it behind your eyes.',15595),
(833,1,5,'',15595),
(834,0,0,'I\'m great at what I do, don\'t get me wrong, but this is ridiculous! What am I supposed to do, build sand castles?',15595),
(835,1,0,'You wouldn\'t think it from a guy like my boss Gazlowe, but he always seemed to know the score. \"Don\'t be afraid to take that big step,\" he said.$B$BHarpies won\'t stop bothering us and the caravans won\'t stop being attacked unless we do something about it, eh?',15595),
(836,1,0,'',15595),
(837,1,0,'Though they do possess some intelligence and some organization, I find it constantly amazing that the quilboars were able to capture and hold so much territory in Kalimdor. Perhaps they are more crafty an enemy than I give them credit for...',15595),
(838,1,0,NULL,15595),
(840,1,0,'What do you want, pup? If you\'re not here for recruitment, I don\'t have time for you.',15595),
(841,1,0,'Well, have you got the ten water pouches?',15595),
(842,1,0,'Well well well, what do we have here? Has Kargal deemed me worthy of another recruit?',15595),
(843,1,0,'Many innocent tauren lost their lives or were forced off their ancestral birthplace when the dwarves of Bael Modan arrived. My land must be reclaimed!',15595),
(844,1,0,'Have you collected the plainstrider beaks? ',15595),
(845,1,0,'How many zhevra have you slain?',15595),
(846,1,0,'I see you are back, $N.$B$BWhile Khazgorm\'s death might delay the digging in my ancestral lands some, it will by no means bring a total end to the destruction.$B$BThe Keep at Bael Modan is an increasing military threat. Built to defend the dig site, it is now poised for offensive force as well.$B$BIf you have the ingredients I requested, I can fashion a charge that will make the hasty dwarves reconsider their actions here in the Barrens.',15595),
(847,1,0,NULL,15595),
(848,1,0,'Do you have the spores, $N? There is a concoction I must send to my associate in Thunder Bluff, which requires the spores...',15595),
(849,1,0,'Once the dwarven flying machine has been destroyed I will feel the sweet satisfaction of revenge.',15595),
(850,1,0,'Hello, $N. Do you have Barak\'s Head for me?',15595),
(851,1,0,'Did you find Verog, $N?',15595),
(852,1,0,'Is Hezrul defeated, $N?',15595),
(853,1,0,'You have something from Apothecary Helbrim?',15595),
(854,1,0,NULL,15595),
(855,1,0,'How goes your hunting, $N?',15595),
(857,5,0,'Where is the Tear of the Moons? I need it now! Need I say!',15595),
(858,1,0,'Quick, we need to get out of here before someone gets suspicious!',15595),
(860,1,0,NULL,15595),
(861,1,0,'How goes the hunt, $N?',15595),
(863,1,0,'Can I help you?',15595),
(864,1,0,'Welcome back. At least, welcome back if you have returned with a sealed testing kit. Otherwise, I will pretend not to notice your utter incompetence and spare my wrath from you until you do as you have been tasked and accomplish my task.',15595),
(865,1,0,'Did you get the horns, $N? Those things are going to make me a fortune!',15595),
(866,1,0,'Hello, $N. Did you get those root samples?',15595),
(867,1,0,'Cut up enough of them yet? Keep slicing and taking trophies. I want 8 Witchwing talons.',15595),
(868,1,0,'Be careful with the eggs you find, $N. If they break, they be no good to me.',15595),
(869,1,0,'Do you have those heads, $N?',15595),
(870,1,0,NULL,15595),
(871,1,0,'The longer it takes to stop these attacks, the harder it will be to provide supplies for the people of the Crossroads.',15595),
(872,1,0,'Cut off the head of their leader, and chaos ensues, $N. Learn this lesson well. It will aid you in the future.$B$BThe boars will flounder without direction, and we will be able to take back the Barrens.',15595),
(873,1,0,'Fear not the waters, $R.',15595),
(874,1,0,NULL,15595),
(875,1,0,'Do you have 6 Harpy Lieutenant Rings yet? Justice must be dealt to them for their vicious attacks on the Horde.',15595),
(876,1,0,'You\'re not getting anything until I see Serena\'s head.',15595),
(877,1,0,'Have you been to the Stagnant Oasis? Was there a fissure beneath its waters?',15595),
(878,1,0,'More information <snort> for the Horde when you\'ve killed the Bristleback\'s wise ones, $R. <snort> Not a moment earlier! Mangletooth is no fool.',15595),
(879,1,0,'How goes your hunt, $R? <snort>$B$BThork thinks he knows the truth about who leads the raids against his people, <snort> but he shall learn how wrong he is if you are successful.$B$BMy death is inescapable, but you have caused great pain to my enemies, so Mangletooth regrets nothing. <snort>',15595),
(880,1,0,'How goes your collection? Did you get the shells?',15595),
(881,1,0,'The great cat calls to you, $N.',15595),
(882,1,0,'$N, have you bested Ishamuhale?',15595),
(883,1,0,'$N, when you approached I saw a new power in your stride. Tell me -- has your spirit met with the great Lakota\'mani?',15595),
(884,1,0,'$N, there is a new power behind your eyes! You have met with the mighty Owatanka, have you not?',15595),
(885,1,0,'There is new resolve within you, $N. A resolve born from pain...$B$BAre you burdened with the death of Washte Pawne?',15595),
(886,1,0,NULL,15595),
(887,1,0,'I don\'t even want to think about the profits I\'ve lost from pirate raiding, and now they set up camp on my doorstep? It\'s getting out of hand, Undermine\'s got to do something about it.',15595),
(888,1,0,'Did you find my things, $N?',15595),
(889,1,0,'Bring Mangletooth 10 blood shards and I will bless you with great speed. You will run with zhevra and the wind will be jealous of you.$B$BIt will not last long, but it should be enough to help you travel throughout the Barrens.',15595),
(890,1,0,'Wares to send on the next ship, $N?',15595),
(891,1,0,'My fleet is in peril with Captain Fairmount and her damned cannoneers blasting away from Northwatch Hold. I want her soldiers to pay as well. Fill my hand with medals from their dead and I will know that vengeance has been given to my fallen privateers.',15595),
(892,1,0,'So, what did Dizzywig have to say?',15595),
(893,1,0,'I, too, have doubts that the pathetic quilboars could attain any level of skill in the area of smithing, but I do as the Warchief commands, and I shall learn what I can about the Razormane tribe.$B$BI have had more menial tasks, and I do so willingly if it aids the orc people.',15595),
(894,1,0,NULL,15595),
(895,1,0,'What\'s happening? Something I can help you with? Goods to ship, perhaps an engineering job?',15595),
(896,1,0,'If only we knew which one of the miners had found the emerald, it\'d be a walk in the park...',15595),
(897,1,0,'You seemed troubled, $N. How go your lessons in the Barrens? Did you find something that disturbs you?',15595),
(898,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(899,1,0,'The quilboar will pay for this, $N. I swear it.',15595),
(900,1,0,'Blinking lights on the control console indicate that the main control valves have not been closed off.',15595),
(901,1,0,'The console lights are dimmed and the gauges and dials all read at their zero positions, everything idling.',15595),
(902,1,0,'Oh, you\'re back, $N! Do you have the samophlange?',15595),
(903,1,0,'How goes your hunt, $N? Have you found the prowlers?',15595),
(905,1,0,'Have you been to the nests, $N?',15595),
(906,1,0,'Yes, what is it?',15595),
(907,1,0,'Are the thunder lizards defeated, $N?',15595),
(908,1,0,'Have you been successful in locating the fathom core? Without it we\'ll have no idea what the Twilight\'s Hammer is exactly up to down there.',15595),
(909,1,0,'Ah, hello again $N. I was just reading the waves the sea, much like I always do. What brings you to the outpost?',15595),
(913,1,0,'Is it done? Have you slain the thunderhawk?',15595),
(914,1,0,'Memories of my nightmares haunt me, $N. Have you defeated the leaders of the fang and acquired their gems?',15595),
(918,1,0,'Do you have the seeds?  I am eager to plant them.',15595),
(919,1,0,'Hello, $N.  Have you found any sprouts near the waters?',15595),
(922,1,0,'Hello...$B$BAnd how may I help you?',15595),
(923,1,0,'Have you been to Wellspring Lake, $N?  Have you been hunting the timberlings there?',15595),
(924,1,0,'The Demon Seed still exists. I can sense its power...',15595),
(926,1,0,'',15595),
(927,1,0,'$N!  You have something for me?',15595),
(929,1,1,'Hello again, $n. Have you completed your task?',15595),
(930,1,0,'$N, you look like you have something to tell me.  Do you have news concerning the timberlings?',15595),
(931,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(932,6,2,'Did you kill Lord Melenas yet? It is vital that he be taken care of quickly and quietly, $N. His continued existence is an embarrassment to us all.',15595),
(933,1,0,'It is good to see you again, $n. I see you have succeeded in collecting the waters of the moonwells on behalf of Corithras Moonrage. I hope you have learned much along the way.',15595),
(934,1,0,'Along with the druids, the Oracle Tree and the Arch $C have been carefully monitoring the growth of Teldrassil. But though we have a new home, our immortal lives have not been restored.',15595),
(935,1,0,'It is good to see you again. I sense that Tarindrella\'s task went smoothly with you by her side.',15595),
(936,1,0,NULL,15595),
(937,1,0,'Their slashing talons and piercing beaks may prove a difficult match for your own abilities, $n, but I have faith that you will not fail in this task.',15595),
(938,1,0,'Mist... It was my fault! The witches caught me off guard... I should not have let them take you...',15595),
(939,1,0,'What is it, $C? You look concerned.',15595),
(940,1,0,'Hmm... You come with the spirit of the forest strongly within you, $C. What business do you have with the Arch Druid of the Kaldorei?',15595),
(941,1,0,'This planter is filled with soil, specially prepared by Denalan.',15595),
(942,1,0,'What ya got there, friend?',15595),
(943,1,0,'With the Stone of Relu I will be able to release the hidden secrets of my fossil as well as Remtravel\'s fossil from Darkshore, $N.',15595),
(944,1,0,'The Master\'s Glaive, $N.$B$BGo there, then speak with me again.',15595),
(945,1,0,'',15595),
(947,1,0,'Do you have my mushrooms, $N? Have you been to the cave?',15595),
(948,1,0,NULL,15595),
(949,1,0,NULL,15595),
(950,1,0,'$N. You return.',15595),
(951,1,0,'$N. Has your rooting through the Ruins of Mathystra been fruitful?',15595),
(952,1,0,'Ah. $C. How may Onu assist you?',15595),
(953,1,0,'When you have studied the tablets and learned of Ameth\'Aran\'s fall, I will take the knowledge on to Auberdine, and inform the Circle of Ancients.',15595),
(954,1,0,NULL,15595),
(955,1,0,'Once I have the earrings, I will cast the spell to search for the whereabouts of the seal that binds me. For centuries I have thought on the freedom destroying the seal would bring to me... Perhaps those centuries have taken a toll upon my mind that I might never recover...',15595),
(956,1,0,'The pillars of this shrine are as the bars of a prison to me, $N. No strength I still possess might break them, and no magic I wield might destroy them...$B$BFor a thousand years and more I have stared at them, wondering if at long last I outlived even the stone, would I be free? Or would it be invisible bars that held me then...',15595),
(957,1,0,'In truth, $N, I am afraid... Afraid that your coming--all of this--is merely a figment of a deranged mind. Can you know the torture that this is? I... Please, you must go quickly.',15595),
(958,1,0,'If only the tools of their undoing could have been destroyed in the cataclysm that destroyed our world... Nonetheless, we must do what we can to ensure that the horrors of our past are not repeated in the future.',15595),
(959,1,0,'The dockmaster has been on my case ever since Mad Magglish made off with that 99-year-old port. I guess that bottle was intended as a gift for Gazlowe from none other than Baron Revilgaz himself.$B$BIf you\'re brave enough and patient enough to seek out Mad Magglish and get that port back, I\'ll see to it you get a nice reward.',15595),
(960,1,0,NULL,15595),
(961,1,0,'',15595),
(962,1,0,'I am eager to see if you can gather enough Serpentbloom from the Wailing Caverns. I\'ve sent many to do my bidding but none have returned.',15595),
(963,1,0,'With a great sorrow in my heart, I followed the Shan\'do Stormrage into hibernation, and took my sorrow to my dreams, sleeping for the passing of thousands of years.',15595),
(964,1,0,'Kill many and kill often, $C - we\'ll need a decent supply of suitable skeletal fragments to make up the outer layer of the key. They don\'t call it a Skeleton Key for nothing, you know.',15595),
(965,1,0,NULL,15595),
(966,1,0,'Have you found any more of their scrolls? I should be able to piece together a larger picture of the cult if you can find them.',15595),
(967,1,0,'You have some business with me, $C?',15595),
(968,1,0,'Hello, $Gsir:madam;.$B$BMay I interest you in one of my tomes?',15595),
(969,1,0,'Bring back da shards, and I be tellin\' you more!',15595),
(970,6,0,'Have you acquired that soul gem?',15595),
(971,1,0,'The journey to Ashenvale is long, and your task is not easy. But if you get me the manuscript, $N...then your reward will be great.',15595),
(973,6,0,'You look a bit shaken up, $n. Are you well?',15595),
(974,1,0,'I\'d go there myself, but... I\'m a little scared of the fire elementals there!',15595),
(975,1,0,'',15595),
(976,1,0,'The Sentinels have a great need for supplies to reinforce themselves in Darkshore.',15595),
(977,1,0,'I\'ve just about finished attaching the fur, $N. Please, hurry back with those horns!',15595),
(980,1,0,NULL,15595),
(981,1,0,NULL,15595),
(982,1,0,'The captains of those ships were good night elves, and they deserve a better fate than they were given. Perhaps tending to their personal effects will be the best way to put their spirits to rest.',15595),
(983,1,0,'Buzzbox 827 sits with an eerie silence. A single flashing light indicates that it needs 6 Crawler Legs to be placed in its holding box.',15595),
(984,1,0,'How goes your search, $N?',15595),
(985,1,0,'Do not stay your hand from what must be done, child. I know how repulsive the idea of killing the creatures of the forest must be, but in this case it is necessary. No cure has been discovered for the corruption let loose upon the forest, and we must do what we can to halt its progress until one is found.',15595),
(986,1,0,'I can\'t in good conscience permit you to seek Volcor until I\'ve crafted that cloak for you.',15595),
(990,1,0,NULL,15595),
(991,1,0,NULL,15595),
(992,6,0,'Welcome back, Junior Surveyor $n!  Have you completed your assignment yet?',15595),
(993,1,0,'',15595),
(994,1,0,'',15595),
(995,1,0,'Yes, $n?',15595),
(996,0,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant.  The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous.  It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(997,6,1,'You have something for me?',15595),
(998,1,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(1000,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1001,1,0,'The machine\'s hatch is open and it seems to wait expectantly for 3 Thresher Eyes to be placed inside.',15595),
(1002,1,0,'Though you have yet to place the 6 Moonstalker Fangs inside, you believe you hear the sounds of static and incoherent gnome ramblings coming from within. Could someone else have fixed the machine already?',15595),
(1003,1,0,'You hear singing coming from Buzzbox 525.$b$b\"Though crawler wine\'s shweet, and thresher ale fine, and moonstalker moonshine ish grand. There\'s nothing sho dear, as a thistle bear beer, and shoon I shall have shome on hand!\"$b$bThe hatch is open and awaits the 4 grizzled scalps as you hear the song repeated over and over.',15595),
(1004,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1007,1,0,'Have you found the statuette, $N?',15595),
(1008,1,0,'We cannot allow the naga to invade our coasts, $N.  It is vital that you go to the Zoram Strand and complete your mission.',15595),
(1009,1,0,'It is said that the Ring of Zoram is the key to any lock within the city. Do you have it, $N?',15595),
(1010,1,0,'Have you gathered the Bathran\'s Hair, $N?  The child\'s health grows weaker by the hour...',15595),
(1011,1,0,'Did you find the camp, $N? Do you have a bottle of disease?',15595),
(1012,1,0,'The anguish of the Dor\'danil druids still haunt my dreams, $N. You must destroy their leaders!',15595),
(1013,1,0,'Did you find the book, $N?',15595),
(1014,1,0,'With Arugal\'s death we stand to increase the Dark Lady\'s stronghold on Lordaeron.',15595),
(1015,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1016,1,0,'Since you must destroy the bracers to kill the elementals, it will probably be difficult to find the specific ones that contain the information the divining scroll needs. You can trade bracers with others in order to obtain the ones you need, or perhaps you have the divined paper already?',15595),
(1017,1,0,'Is it done? Is Sarilus Foulborne dead?',15595),
(1018,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1019,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1020,1,0,'I must apologize, for I have no time to speak.  My child, Relara, is deathly ill!',15595),
(1021,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1022,1,0,'The tome of the shrine is a mysterious object. It is not a book in the traditional sense. The leaves of the tome were blessed by Mel\'Thandris herself, and records events of import in its pages.$B$BIt is hard for me to explain. If you go to the shrine, you will understand.',15595),
(1023,2,0,'Ah, welcome back, $N.',15595),
(1024,1,0,'Hello. How are you?',15595),
(1025,1,0,'The furbolg were not always our enemy, $N. But times change, and it is no longer a time of peace here in these dark woods.',15595),
(1026,1,0,'It upsets me so that the treants have become corrupt. I wish I could do more to help them.',15595),
(1027,1,0,'Did you find the final piece of the rod, $N?',15595),
(1028,1,0,'You can sense a subtle yet powerful force within the shrine and surrounding trees.$B$BYou begin placing the rod within the shrine and a soft thrumming noise emits from around you as the shrine begins to glow...',15595),
(1029,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1030,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1031,1,0,'Have you found them? What did Anilia say? Where is she?',15595),
(1032,1,0,'Please, help me avenge Anilia\'s death.',15595),
(1033,1,0,'$N, did you find Iris Lake? Do you have the Tear?',15595),
(1034,1,0,'Do you yet have the Stardust, $N?',15595),
(1035,1,0,'Did you face the Shadethicket Oracle, $N? If so, then please hand me the fallen moonstone. Relara has strength left for only a few more breaths!',15595),
(1036,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1037,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1038,1,0,'What\'d you find out?',15595),
(1039,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1040,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1041,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1042,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1043,1,0,'The woods are perilous for the unprepared. Keep your weapons close at hand and your wits even closer, or your next journey into the haunted forest may be your last.',15595),
(1044,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1045,1,0,'Have you slain Ran yet, my friend?$B$BEven the Night elves do not truly deserve his wrath. His hatred burns even brighter than my own, but his mind is no longer his own. He is a threat to all the natural creatures of this forest.',15595),
(1046,1,0,'The Sentinels do what they can here in Ashenvale, but it\'s thanks to $rs like you that we have gained the ground we have.',15595),
(1047,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1048,1,0,'Perhaps I was not explicit in my orders, $c. I want High Inquisitor Whitemane killed once and for all. And while you\'re at it, take out her top brass as well.$B$BKill that zealot, Scarlet Commander Mograine. Lay waste to Herod, the Scarlet Champion. And slaughter Houndmaster Loksey and his filthy mutts too.$B$BNow begone!',15595),
(1049,1,0,'Cairne is a brave and noble leader and I would trust him with my own life. But it is others that I do not trust in this political climate.$b$bOnce I have a chance to gather all the knowledge available I can provide sound council to the Chieftain.$b$bHave you had a chance to travel to Tirisfal Glades? To the Scarlet Monastery? The Compendium of the Fallen is just one piece in this complicated puzzle...',15595),
(1050,1,0,'The Monastery was a seminary for Paladins-in-training. Once a stronghold of the Light, it fell into the hands of the crazed zealots of the Scarlet Crusade.$b$bThe Crusade believed their goal a noble one: to purify the land of the undead plague. But insanity tainted their plight and now they stand enemies to all.$b$bBring Mythology of the Titans to me so I can study it and house it here in Ironforge.$b$bThe corrupt halls of the Monastery are no place for such a historical treasure.',15595),
(1051,1,0,'What do you want, stranger?',15595),
(1052,6,0,'Who goes there? What do you want from me?',15595),
(1053,1,5,'The corruption in the Monastery will not end until the highest ranking officials have been removed.$b$bIn the name of the Light, slay High Inquisitor Whitemane, Scarlet Commander Mograine,  Herod, the Scarlet Champion and Houndmaster Loksey. Once they have fallen, perhaps the true cause can be rekindled. Until then, anyone who crosses the path of the Crusade lies in peril.$b$bVenture forth from Southshore and make it so!',15595),
(1054,1,2,'The furbolgs\' corruption has caused Ashenvale to become a fraction of its former glory.',15595),
(1055,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1056,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1057,1,0,'There is much work to be done before the Charred Vale can be restored to the lush forest it once was.$B$BClear the area of those foul menaces, $N! Only then can we begin to reclaim what belongs to nature.',15595),
(1058,1,0,'Look at our poor little elf friends. All caged up with no forest to frolic in!$b$bNow were you able to find me some sap? How about the whiskers from the twilight runners? Don\'t suppose you have that fey dragon scale on you?$b$bAnd eyes! I\'ll need so many eyes! You just can\'t mix up a fierce forest magic brew without a good helping of eyes!',15595),
(1059,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1060,1,0,'You seem a shady character. You have something for me to see?',15595),
(1061,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1062,1,0,'The Greatwood Vale lies to the northwest, $N. Go. Strike fear into those who would pillage this land!',15595),
(1063,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1064,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1065,1,0,'Ah, are you here with my new test subjects?',15595),
(1066,1,0,'Did you find the Syndicate Shadow Mages, and collect from them the blood?',15595),
(1067,1,0,'You have returned, $N. Do you bring aid from Apothecary Lydon?',15595),
(1068,1,0,'The tree spirits wail at the loss of their brethren, $N. You must destroy the shredders XT:4 and XT:9, or I fear Stonetalon will never be healed.',15595),
(1069,1,0,'Did you get the eggs, $N? I already made a shipping deal with Wharfmaster Dizzywig!',15595),
(1070,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1071,1,0,'How goes the battle on your end, $N?',15595),
(1072,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1073,1,0,'I can\'t make any Nitromirglyceronium if I don\'t have the potions... they\'re vital to its creation.',15595),
(1074,1,0,'Ah, goodie goodie, you\'re back.',15595),
(1075,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1076,1,0,'Hello, $N. Have you found the component I need?',15595),
(1077,1,0,'Haha! you\'re back! Do you have it? Do you have the spell?',15595),
(1078,1,2,'Hello again, $N.$B$BHave you already returned from the Vale in Stonetalon with those scales?',15595),
(1079,1,0,'Did you get the plans, $N?',15595),
(1080,1,0,'How\'d it go, $N?',15595),
(1081,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1082,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1083,1,0,'The first time I saw the Charred Vale I almost wept, $N.',15595),
(1084,1,0,'I have a feeling Gaxim will find a use for the shrapnel regardless of how the Venture Co. has used it in the past.',15595),
(1085,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1086,1,0,'You must find the Venture Company airport if it exists, $N.',15595),
(1087,1,0,'Here, channeling magic is like drawing water from a well with a bucket full of holes.',15595),
(1088,1,0,'When my master bade me to the peak of Stonetalon, I expected that all I would need was to lay waste to the night elves that crawled the sacred ruins of our ancient temple of Azshara, their touch despoiling its sanctity... but Ordanus had slipped my grasp.',15595),
(1089,1,0,'Three keyholes are carved into the stone.',15595),
(1090,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1091,1,0,'Yes, $N? What can I do for you?',15595),
(1092,1,0,'Something I can help you with?',15595),
(1093,1,0,'Did you find those plans? I\'m eager to impress the new boss. Hopefully, once he\'s convinced of my loyalty--well, as much as he can be convinced... goblin\'s honor, you know?--he\'ll feel comfortable making use of my rather impressive genius.',15595),
(1094,1,0,'Hello there! How can I help you?',15595),
(1095,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1096,1,0,'Sputtervalve will want some sort of proof that Gerenzo\'s dead. I think his mechanical arm will probably do.',15595),
(1097,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1098,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1100,1,0,'From your look of concern, I can tell that something is amiss....',15595),
(1104,1,0,'Hi hi hi! Did you get that venom??',15595),
(1105,1,0,'My brother is making progress with his new fuel design, and that has me worried. I need to start work on a tortoise shell fuel tank as soon as possible!',15595),
(1106,1,0,'Well, you found me. Good for you.$b$bAre you here about that axe I made for Gath\'Ilzogg? Or are you here to reclaim Duchess Pamay\'s honor?$b$bActually, I don\'t care which it is. If you\'re here to fight, then let\'s get it over with...',15595),
(1107,0,0,'Do you have the tail fins?  If I can\'t protect our car from its own speed, then it won\'t last long in these races.',15595),
(1108,1,0,'Did you find any indurium flakes, $N. I have my forge heated up and ready to test them.',15595),
(1110,1,0,'$N, have you been out into the Flats? Did you bring back that load of parts I wanted?',15595),
(1111,1,0,'Speak up! Tell me, are you dropping off or picking up?',15595),
(1112,1,0,'Did you make it to Ratchet and get those parts?',15595),
(1113,1,0,'Have you returned from the Scarlet Monastery? I\'ll need many hearts for this delightful experiment!$b$bNo doubt, Varimathras and the Dark Lady will be pleased to be rid of the Scarlet Scum as well...',15595),
(1114,1,0,'You have something for me? That\'s great! let\'s see it!',15595),
(1115,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1116,1,0,'Back so soon? Do you have my dream dust?',15595),
(1117,1,0,'Did you get anything on Nazz Steamboil? Anything he might want to keep a secret??',15595),
(1118,1,0,'Hello hello. And what brings a noble $R such as you down to Booty Bay?',15595),
(1119,1,0,'Hello, $N. Was Fizzlebub able to help us?',15595),
(1120,1,0,'Hi! You have something for me?',15595),
(1121,1,0,'What are you looking at?',15595),
(1122,1,0,'Hello $N. How\'d that stout work out? It\'s strong stuff, isn\'t it?',15595),
(1123,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1124,1,0,'This is a dangerous land to be so casual, $C. What brings you to the wastes of Silithus?',15595),
(1125,1,1,'Alliance or Horde, it doesn\'t matter - no being deserves to be trapped on this world as a tortured spirit.  The freeing of these souls will make things right, $N.',15595),
(1126,1,0,'Well, did it work? You\'re still in one piece, which is good news. Did you find anything?',15595),
(1127,1,0,'Do you have those Zanzil mixtures yet, $N?',15595),
(1130,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1131,1,0,'Have you defeated the foul Steelsnap, $N?',15595),
(1132,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1133,1,2,NULL,15595),
(1134,1,0,'Do you have the pridewing venom sacs, $N? We cannot allow the orcs to use the beasts\' poisons against us!',15595),
(1135,1,0,'Did you find Highperch, $N? Any luck with the wyverns there?',15595),
(1136,1,0,'Have you been to the Alterac Mountains, $N? Did you face the elusive Frostmaw?',15595),
(1137,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1138,1,0,'...lemon crab, whipper root crab, and Ironforge surprise crab.  That\'s about it.$B$BOh, hello there $N.  Do you have them fine crab chunks I was telling you about?',15595),
(1140,1,1,'I heard whisper once that the satyrs\' history is somehow related to that of the night elves, but I have found my esteemed hosts reticent to speak of the matter.',15595),
(1141,1,0,'There\'s plenty of good dishes you use Darkshore groupers for.  They\'re good to eat, but I think it\'s more fun catching them.$B$BYou caught any Darkshore groupers yet?',15595),
(1143,1,0,'Athrikus Narassin is an ancient and powerful warlock. Perhaps we should wait for Delgren\'s assistance, but he obviously had much faith in you to send you alone.',15595),
(1145,1,0,'I envy you, $C. You have the look of someone who\'s been outside the walls of Orgrimmar for a while.$B$BI myself would travel in the name of the Warchief if Thrall didn\'t have need of my skills here in the city. But he leads us well, and I trust his judgement - I remain here for as long as he needs me.',15595),
(1146,1,0,'War brings my group and I to the Shimmering Flats, $C. What brings you here?',15595),
(1147,1,0,'With the amount of travelers heading out to the Flats for those races, I\'m sure we can convince enough adventure seekers to help push back those insects. My party and I won\'t be able to leave until we do.',15595),
(1148,1,0,'Ah, it been a long time since you\'ve come to see me, $N. What can I do for you today? You be looking like you\'ve seen the face of battle recently. Good... good for the Horde and good for you. The more battle you\'ve seen, the more helpful you\'ll be; stronger, too.',15595),
(1149,1,0,'Faith. It is far more important than some realize.$B$BIt does not matter what you believe sometimes. It is just important that you believe in something.',15595),
(1150,1,0,'You must be prepared spiritually, physically and mentally for the challenges that lie ahead of you.$b$bToo often do we rush forward before we are ready. I consider it my duty to the youth, no matter which tribe they belong to, to prepare them for the dangers they may face after they leave the sanctity of their home.',15595),
(1151,1,0,'Rok\'Alim is also called the Pounder by the centaur tribes in Thousand Needles because of the thundering his fists make as he pummels the creatures brave, or stupid, enough to stand in his path.',15595),
(1152,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1153,1,0,'I saw the travelers again - the ones that would not sell me a sample of the ore. I spit at them for not helping the warchief.$B$BMay they die in battle like cowards and not like warriors as should be the right of all people who ally themselves with the Horde.',15595),
(1154,1,0,'Bring me the book after you\'ve studied it. I will not ask you your question until after you have given me the book.',15595),
(1159,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1160,1,0,'I hope you made the Scarlet Crusade suffer some before stealing the book from them.$b$bMy views of their kind are not unwarranted. The Crusade may have been followers of the Light at one time, but now, they seek to destroy any creatures that have not sided with their religion. They believe all undead, Forsaken or otherwise, must be cleansed, and those traveling in their lands must either be insane, or subject to the undead\'s powerful magics. Idiots. Idiots and fools; all of them.',15595),
(1164,5,0,'Kill them all and bring me their heads!',15595),
(1166,0,0,'Me thirsty for grog. Me miss snuff too. Where is strongbox? You go get for Overlord Mok\'Morokk.$b$bGo find south in old home. Me too busy leading ogres to get.',15595),
(1167,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1168,1,0,'Mok\'Morokk tell all ogres to stay and keep this place safe. Me think ogres need to kill black dragon army and get old home back.$b$bYou help ogres get home back. Help ogres get revenge.',15595),
(1169,0,0,'With the hearts and tongues of scorched offspring of the black dragon army, I can decipher what wretched beast introduced her spawn into our home. Perhaps with a greater knowledge of our aggressors, we can seek to destroy them once and for all and reclaim Stonemaul Village from ruin.$b$bOf course, convincing Mok\'Morokk to move his lethargic, fat mass out of this muck hole is going to be an epic quest in and of itself...',15595),
(1170,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1171,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1172,1,0,'You must hurry to the Dragonmurk, $n. With Onyxia\'s eggs riddled around the Wyrmbog, we face overwhelming numbers unless something is done quickly.$b$bDestroy her eggs! Don\'t let the black dragon plague spread across our homeland!',15595),
(1173,1,0,'I thought you were going to attempt to drive Mok\'Morokk out of the village. Instead you have come to me to chat?',15595),
(1175,1,0,'It\'s bad enough having to clear out the wreckage of the racers without having to pick them out of burnt animal parts.',15595),
(1176,6,0,'Do you have those bones for me? I was just about to start working on lightening the steering rig, but I don\'t want to open her up without all the parts I need.',15595),
(1177,0,0,'Gimme food or me eat you.',15595),
(1178,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1179,1,0,'Watch where you\'re stepping!  Watch watch watch!!  This is delicate stuff you see here, and if we\'re to win then it must all work perfectly!',15595),
(1180,1,0,'',15595),
(1181,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1182,1,0,'Much as I hate to admit it, that gnome team they have out there is pretty good. Our boys need every edge they can get.',15595),
(1183,1,0,'$N! Did you manage to track down the fuel regulator?',15595),
(1184,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1185,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1186,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1187,6,0,'How\'m I supposed to show my face around the track without a little extra kick to get me going? It\'s a travesty, I tell you.',15595),
(1188,1,0,'As I\'m sure you know, the Gizmorium can service all of your tinkering needs! How can I help you?',15595),
(1189,1,0,'Can you believe Pozzik put a bucket of sand on the racer? How am I supposed to hit my maximum speed with a bucket of sand under the seat?',15595),
(1190,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1191,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1192,1,0,'I\'d like to integrate indurium into different parts of our racers, but I need large amounts of raw indurium to create these parts.$B$BYou can find indurium ore in the Uldaman excavation in the Badlands, across the sea in Khaz Modan.$B$BThe gnomes are getting their own supply of it, so it\'s important we get our own to keep pace with them.',15595),
(1193,1,0,'A large, broken trap lies before you. From the looks of it, the ogres have tried to repair the trap but to no avail. A hastily written note lies next to the trap, and strangely enough it details exactly what is needed to repair it: a thorium widget and some frost oil. Were the trap repaired, an ogre passing near it might get trapped, and could be avoided.$b$bClearly, it would seem fortuitous that very few ogres know how to read.$b$bClearly.',15595),
(1194,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1195,1,0,'Once we have the filled phial, we can send it along to my associate, Rau, in the Thousand Needles. He was the one who requested the phial of water, so he\'ll better know how we can make use of it.',15595),
(1196,1,0,'I don\'t suppose you\'ve been sent by Zangen, hm?',15595),
(1197,1,0,'I am eager to put my hands upon the Cloven Hoof. Have you taken it yet?',15595),
(1198,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1199,1,0,'Blackfathom Deeps was once an ancient night elf temple. It once housed a most powerful moonwell. Who knows what evil brews there now at the hands of the Twilight\'s Hammer.$B$BHave you made any progress in ridding their presence?',15595),
(1200,1,0,'Time is a precious commodity, $C.$B$BMy role here in Darnassus is to ensure that the Argent Dawn thrives and that the evil forces encroaching upon Kalimdor are thwarted.$B$BState your business quickly or be on your way.',15595),
(1201,1,0,'Did you find the infiltrators, $N?',15595),
(1202,0,0,'Did you find the documents, $N?  They hold information vital to the stability of the Alliance and, hence, vital to the security of the Horde.',15595),
(1203,1,0,'You have my blade??',15595),
(1204,1,0,'Did you get the forked tongues?',15595),
(1205,0,0,'Do you have the tooth of Deadmire, $N?  Have you ended the creature\'s suffering?',15595),
(1206,1,0,'Where are those eyes?',15595),
(1218,6,0,'Spice.  We could all use some spice in our life.  You agree?',15595),
(1219,1,0,'Do you have a report to make?',15595),
(1220,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(1222,1,0,'Have you seen Mr. Ignatz? I sent him into the swamp some time ago and he hasn\'t returned!',15595),
(1238,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(1239,1,0,'You have another matter to report, $N?',15595),
(1240,1,0,'There is an angry spirit about you, $gbrother:sister;. What brings you to Kin\'weelay?',15595),
(1241,1,0,'Hmph, you better have good reason to interrupt a man and his fishin\'. I don\'t take kindly to peddlers, let alone beggars.',15595),
(1242,1,0,'Hello, $N. Is there something I can do for you? Perhaps you\'d like to try some of our special Trias cheddar? Or a block of Darnassian bleu?',15595),
(1243,1,0,'Not too safe to be traveling about in the woods, $N. Be careful, and if you see anything suspicious or dangerous, contact the Watchers immediately. Don\'t try and take anything on yourself. We\'re not responsible for anything terrible that might happen to you.$B$BBut we both know you\'re gonna ignore me and fight whatever comes out of the darkness anyway, don\'t we? Haha, yeah, you adventurer types... all the same.',15595),
(1244,1,0,'Be careful out there, $N. I know Trias was the one to send you here, but that doesn\'t mean there isn\'t anything lurking out in the woods that couldn\'t cause you some trouble... especially with you investigating the Defias.',15595),
(1245,1,0,'I see you\'re back, and in one piece. We both know you\'re not here for cheese, so let\'s cut out the pleasantries. Was Backus any help, or have you even left for Duskwood yet?',15595),
(1246,14,0,NULL,15595),
(1247,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1248,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1249,1,0,'Did he slip away? He looked a little shady the way he was watching us.',15595),
(1250,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1251,6,0,'What\'s that you have there, $n? Evidence from the remains of the Shady Rest Inn?',15595),
(1252,1,0,'Have you found anything of interest at the Shady Rest Inn?',15595),
(1253,1,0,'Have you found evidence from the site of the Shady Rest Inn?',15595),
(1258,1,0,'My research with the Mudrock tongues is progressing nicely. I trust your crab hunt goes well?',15595),
(1259,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1260,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1261,1,0,'$N, did you discover Marg\'s fate?',15595),
(1262,1,0,'You traveled from Brackenwall Village in Dustwallow? How fares Nazeer, and how fare his efforts in the marsh?',15595),
(1264,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1265,1,0,'Yes, $N?',15595),
(1266,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1267,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1268,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1269,6,0,'Have you found any leads on what happened at the Shady Rest Inn?',15595),
(1270,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1271,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1273,1,0,'Did you find Reethe?',15595),
(1274,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1275,1,0,'Once I have enough samples to study, my true work can begin. With the corrupted brain stems of both the satyr and naga of Blackfathom Deeps I can try to draw a correlation between the mutations.$B$BPerhaps with that gained knowledge we can prevent the blood elves from delving deeper into deformity and evil.',15595),
(1276,3,0,'Hello there, $c. Something I can help you with?',15595),
(1282,1,0,'',15595),
(1284,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1285,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1286,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1287,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1288,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1289,1,0,'',15595),
(1301,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1302,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1318,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1319,1,0,'Something for me to look at?',15595),
(1320,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1321,0,0,'Something for me, $c?',15595),
(1322,0,0,'Did you get them sacs from the spiders?',15595),
(1323,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1324,1,0,'Hello again, $N. I hope you don\'t mind the assistance, but we couldn\'t have Hendel escaping, or worse, wind up dead.',15595),
(1338,1,0,'A letter from the dwarven lands? I wonder who would call from so far to the north...$B$BPlease, let me see the order.',15595),
(1339,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1358,1,0,'You have a package for me?',15595),
(1359,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(1361,1,0,'I note that your task is unfinished, $N. Shall I inform Sharlindra of your ineptitude?',15595),
(1362,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1363,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1364,1,0,'What brings you to Nethergarde Keep, $R?',15595),
(1365,1,0,'$N, have you defeated Khan Dez\'hepah?',15595),
(1366,1,0,'How is your collection of ears, $N? Large?',15595),
(1367,1,0,'Leave! The Magram do not speak with the weak. We kill them!$B$BIf you want to speak with me, then show me you are strong. Return after you slay many Gelkis.',15595),
(1368,1,0,'Your two feet step on Gelkis earth. You are not welcome here!$B$BProve you seek friendship with the Gelkis. Kill Magram centaur. Return when the ground is wet with Magram blood.',15595),
(1369,1,0,'If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!',15595),
(1370,1,0,'Return after you further prove your worth to the Gelkis!',15595),
(1371,1,0,'If you are not our enemy, then you will do what I ask!',15595),
(1372,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1373,0,0,'Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, $N.',15595),
(1374,1,0,'Show me you are a friend of the Gelkis, $N.',15595),
(1375,1,0,'Do tasks for the Magram, and I will help you.',15595),
(1380,1,0,'Is Khan Hratha dead? Do you have the key fragment?',15595),
(1381,1,0,'Do what I ask.  Prove to me that you are an ally of the Magram!',15595),
(1382,1,0,'Be gone! The Gelkis do not want you here. Leave now!!$B$BReturn after killing many Magram, and then I will speak with you.',15595),
(1383,1,0,'That Infiltrator in Stonard will surely.... open up... after he drinks my special serum. Haha!$b$bThe ingredients required are by no means easy to procure. Shadow Panthers are common in the Swamp but collecting enough hearts for our purpose can be daunting. And the Mire Lord can be such a fussy beast.$b$b',15595),
(1384,1,0,'You have the charms? You showed the Kolkar they are weak?',15595),
(1385,1,0,'You will go now, or the Magram will crush you! To be our friend, you must kill Gelkis.',15595),
(1386,1,0,'Are you afraid of the Kolkar? Why do you not kill them? Maybe you forgot how to kill. Hurry and kill Kolkar before they are dead!',15595),
(1387,1,0,'Do you have a report, $N?',15595),
(1388,1,0,'I hope you have proven yourself of use to our dear friend, Apothecary Faustin.',15595),
(1389,1,0,'Do you have the crystals?',15595),
(1390,1,0,'NULL',15595),
(1391,1,0,'Please have mercy on me! I have information that goes beyond alliance boundaries. While I am no sympathizer of the Horde, there is political treachery going on that must be revealed!',15595),
(1392,0,0,'Greetings.  And welcome to the Harborage.',15595),
(1393,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1394,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1395,1,0,'Hello! Don\'t mind all the commotion, it\'s just business as usual at Nethergarde Keep.$B$BYou have something for me?',15595),
(1396,1,0,'The swamp creatures press close, $N. Please, you must defend the camp!',15595),
(1398,1,0,'Did you find any driftwood, $N?',15595),
(1418,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1419,0,0,'Do you have the jawbones?',15595),
(1420,1,0,'You returned. You have a report?',15595),
(1421,1,0,'Do you have the wizard\'s reagents, $N?',15595),
(1422,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1423,1,0,'You have something for me?',15595),
(1424,1,0,'No one knows what dark practices went on inside The Temple of Atal\'Hakkar. But we do know that great and powerful forces of magic were used.$b$bWe must learn as much as we can about such magic. Perhaps the spells of the Atal\'ai will prove of use to the Horde.$b$bOnce you have gathered enough Atal\'ai artifacts from around the Pool of Tears, I can begin to understand what the trolls were hoping to accomplish and what went so horribly wrong.',15595),
(1425,1,0,'You have business with me?',15595),
(1426,1,0,'I am patient. Patient and everlasting like an old kank stone from Draenor. The fish men shall not make it past our borders--not while I still stand. If we had an army at our disposal I would cleanse this world and all others of their presence. I feel my hatred seethe just speaking about them.',15595),
(1427,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1428,1,0,'Not until the sea and all her children are silenced will I be pleased... especially those disgusting fish men.',15595),
(1429,1,0,'You are brave to come here. Brave or foolish...',15595),
(1430,0,0,'I have a cask of wine waiting for your success, $N. It\'s only right I taste the goods before I have it shipped back to my customers.',15595),
(1431,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1432,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1433,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1434,1,0,'I was warned by a tauren companion that the satyr are not all they appear to be. He believes there is something more to them, that their evil is a twisting of their true nature. But I have not seen such things.$B$BI see only the ruthless slaughter of the weak and the corruption of those who seek dark power.$B$BI will continue in my duty of annihilating them until the Warchief directs me otherwise. Until then, I take no pity on them.',15595),
(1435,1,0,'I have tried to make the magics as simple as possible. Drawing the spirit of your victim out of its injured form should be child\'s play. Do not rely on the gem\'s power to slay your foe completely. You must only activate the gem when they are close to death, or it will be useless.',15595),
(1436,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1437,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1438,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1439,1,0,'I fear Tyranis will attempt to learn the Burning Blade\'s secrets and count himself among their kind if they allow it - he has always adored the power magic brings to those who are seduced by it.$B$BI\'m not sure I could endure returning home to my family with news of Tyranis\' spirit flirting with such dangers. It\'s a terrible enough crime among my kind to pursue such things, but to become that which we attempt to protect ourselves from, well, that\'s apprehensible.',15595),
(1440,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1444,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1447,11,0,'I didn\'t mean anything by the comment \'bout you being a stupid $C. We\'re friends, right? No hard feelings?',15595),
(1448,1,0,'I have traveled the world from the jungles of Azeroth to the snowy peaks of Khaz Modan.$B$BNever before have I asked for help in my adventures. But my old bones are tired.$B$BNothing would leave me feeling more satisfied than knowing that I completed my final quest for the Explorers\' League$B$BIf you\'d be so kind as to help me search for the Temple of Atal\'Hakkar, $C, I\'d greatly appreciate it.$B$BScour the Swamp of Sorrows and report back with your findings!',15595),
(1449,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1450,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1451,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1452,1,0,'Ya ever had a Rhapsody Malt? One of my finest brews, if I do say so myself. Hiccup!$B$BBut if I\'m gonna relive the horrors of that fateful flight over... hiccup... the swamp, well I\'m gonna need me something a wee bit stronger. Hiccup!$B$BDon\'t suppose you found me those gizzards and livers I need to add that extra kick to my Kalimdor Kocktail?$B$BHiccup!',15595),
(1453,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1454,1,0,'',15595),
(1455,1,0,'',15595),
(1456,1,0,'No offense to whoever Nijel is, but this camp ain\'t the most comfortable place I\'ve spent a night, if you know what I mean, $N.',15595),
(1457,1,0,'Business is booming, $N, and I don\'t have a lot of time for questions. If you\'ve got business with the Reclaimers, then let\'s hear it. If not, I\'m gonna have to ask you to talk to one of me underlings - they\'re adept enough at taking care of things \'round here.',15595),
(1458,1,0,'Despicable creatures, the satyr. Story says they\'re somehow tied to the night elves, but I\'m not so sure I believe it.$B$BI think they get that on account of that one elf that brought them into the war few years back. World\'s never been the same since. Lot more dangerous, and a lot scarier.',15595),
(1459,1,0,'Sorry I couldn\'t tell you where to find the kodo or the scorpashi. I\'m not terribly familiar with the area, and I haven\'t had time to explore.',15595),
(1465,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1466,1,0,'I didn\'t even realize these demon things were in Desolace. Last I read, centaur pretty much owned the land after the night elves picked up and left years ago.$B$BI wonder why they took up here, and how.',15595),
(1467,1,0,'Well met, $N. Business is booming, the sounds of anvils being struck rings throughout Ironforge, the bellows blow the fires hot, and me wife\'s making me a pie for dessert after tonight\'s dinner. Could life be any grander?',15595),
(1469,1,0,'At long last you have returned, $N. It has been quite some time since we last spoke. I thought perhaps you had forgotten about my quest.$B$BDid you locate that wily gryphon rider? Did he have anything to report?',15595),
(1477,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1480,1,0,'The Burning Blade begin to realize how weak they truly are. Their magics are pathetic, their strength feeble.$B$BTheir only power comes from those they serve, and not from any understanding of true power and knowledge.',15595),
(1481,1,0,'Do not bring me an incorrect scalp, $c. Using the incorrect reagents could cause our deaths. The demon lord may have contingency spells on his person to slay those who would scry upon him.$B$BFate has already dealt me enough pain.',15595),
(1482,1,0,'I am ready for the oracle crystal, $c. Finding and destroying this Lord Azrethoc would garner a great deal of favor with the Warchief for both of us. We would do well to work together and to do so swiftly so we may further our own ends and curry favor with the Warchief. ',15595),
(1483,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1484,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1486,1,0,'I am very interested in examining the hides from the deviate creatures who have infested these caves. Have you had any luck in collecting some, $C?',15595),
(1487,1,0,'$N, we, the Disciples of Naralex, need your help. Our numbers are dwindling with our master trapped in his twisted nightmare. We have not the forces necessary to deal with the corrupt creatures which now haunt these caverns.$b$bI beg of you, enter the caves and wage war on the deviate creatures!',15595),
(1488,1,0,'Glory to the Horde, and death to our enemies, $N!$B$BThe demons in Desolace pose a greater threat than ever before. My hope of returning to the Warchief dwindles as more and more of the foul creatures seem to appear.$B$BI sometimes wish it was only the centaur we had to deal with.',15595),
(1489,1,0,'Your masters are fools to send you here, for I will never again be a Scourge slave!',15595),
(1490,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1491,1,0,'Where is my wailing essence?',15595),
(1492,1,0,'You seek passage on the next ship, or have some item you wish to send aboard it?',15595),
(1514,1,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(1560,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1578,1,0,'I have no time to chat. Do you have business with me?',15595),
(1581,1,0,'Hello, $N. Do you have the elixirs to trade?',15595),
(1582,1,0,'Greetings, $N.',15595),
(1618,1,0,'I hope you\'re here with good news from Ironforge.  Because I\'m at my wit\'s end!',15595),
(1655,1,0,'So, any luck yet? Haha, those ogres didn\'t get the best of ya yet, did they?',15595),
(1690,1,0,'Back so soon? I hope you were able to bring some goblin-style justice to those Wastewander Bandits and Thieves like I asked you to!',15595),
(1691,1,0,'Well, were you able to take out those nomads like I asked? The Gadgetzan Water Company is developing plans based on your success here! Don\'t let us down, now...',15595),
(1707,1,0,'Got the five Wastewander water pouches we need?  If you do, then the Gadgetzan Water Company Care Package, Model 103-XB, will be yours!',15595),
(1789,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1790,1,0,NULL,15595),
(1878,5,0,'Back again, $n?  If you have five more Wastewander water pouches, then I have a care package with your name on it!',15595),
(1918,1,0,'Yeah, what do you need?',15595),
(2038,1,0,'$N! Where are my things?!',15595),
(2039,1,0,'',15595),
(2040,1,0,'Have you found the Gnoam Sprecklesprocket, $N?',15595),
(2041,1,0,'',15595),
(2078,1,0,'Where be me first mate, $N? Shackles n\' sharks fer ye soon if ye don\'t hurry!',15595),
(2098,1,0,'Have ye found me broke down key, landlubber?',15595),
(2118,1,0,'Have you brought me the sick animal, $N?$B$BShould you fail to spring the trap, do not fret - Tharnariun\'s Hope is eternal. If you require another trap, abandon your task and report back to me.',15595),
(2138,1,0,'Is your task complete?',15595),
(2139,1,0,'With the infected Den Mother slain, the population of Rabid Thistle Bears entering our land is lessened. Waste no time, $N.',15595),
(2158,2,0,'',15595),
(2159,6,1,'How might I be of service to you, young one?  Are you here to rest in the inn?  Do you require a hearthstone?',15595),
(2160,1,0,'Hi there! Come in, take a seat by the fire and warm yourself with a flagon of ale.',15595),
(2161,1,0,'Welcome to Razor Hill!',15595),
(2199,1,0,'Have you got the five silver bars I asked for?  I will share my sad tale of woe with you concerning the necklace you now possess... but only after I get those bars!  Please, help a gnome out, won\'t ya?',15595),
(2203,1,0,'Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need?  Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success.  Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...',15595),
(2206,1,0,'Your mortality wanes with every moment you waste loitering in the barracks, $C.',15595),
(2258,1,0,'Have you gotten the things I need yet? You won\'t get paid unless you bring me those reagents.',15595),
(2278,1,0,'The voice of the stone watcher seems to resonate within your very inner being:$b$b\"You must first satisfy the data assimilation prerequisite of Discs of Norgannon; once you fulfill this requirement, you will then be permitted to obtain a portable version of the stored data. Please be sure you have fully explored the information within this repository first.\"',15595),
(2280,1,0,'What is that you have there? What did you learn from the discs?',15595),
(2383,6,0,'What\'s that you have there? A parchment? You\'re not a scholar, I hope...',15595),
(2399,1,0,'',15595),
(2438,6,4,'Please move swiftly. I can only hope that my emerald dreamcatcher has been unharmed by the furbolg.$B$BHave you recovered it yet, $N?',15595),
(2439,1,0,'Welcome to the Vault of Ironforge, $N.  What may I do for you today?',15595),
(2440,1,0,'Greetings, $C! Are you here for alchemy training, or perhaps something else?',15595),
(2459,6,2,'Ferocitas and the Gnarlpine mystics must return what is mine.  Please retrieve the emerald so that I may repair my emerald dreamcatcher.',15595),
(2498,1,0,'',15595),
(2499,1,0,'Have you located Oakenscowl yet, $r?',15595),
(2500,1,0,'Have you gotten the things I need yet?  You won\'t get paid unless you bring me those reagents.',15595),
(2501,1,0,'Have you used the vessels to get me the scorched guardian dragon blood I need?  Yes, I know it is a dangerous task... but the recipe for my restorative brew awaits your success.  Risk and reward, my friend... risk and reward...',15595),
(2518,1,0,'I regret the task that I have asked you to carry out; but Lady Sathrah is beyond hope.$B$BIt is our hope to offer the sacrifice of the spinnerets to Elune. With this sacrifice, Elune will bless Sathrah so that she might be reborn, and at peace.',15595),
(2519,1,0,'',15595),
(2520,1,0,'Have you placed the sacrifice at the fountain, $n?',15595),
(2521,1,0,'I have dedicated my life to the search of flawless draenethyst spheres. A lifetime, tau',15595),
(2522,1,0,'Have you found another flawless draenethyst sphere?',15595),
(2523,1,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(2541,1,0,'If I can examine the charm, I may be able to figure out how to break the enchantment. Have you found one?',15595),
(2561,1,0,'$N, be wary when approaching my physical form; the enchantment it is under is quite powerful.',15595),
(2581,1,0,'You smell foul, $N. Have you been traipsing in sulfur fields? And where are my components?!',15595),
(2582,1,0,'Do you have the beast organs?',15595),
(2583,1,0,'Where are the organs, $N!?',15595),
(2584,1,0,'Where are the organs, $N!?',15595),
(2585,1,0,'Where are the organs, $N!?$b$b',15595),
(2586,1,0,'Where are the organs, $N!?',15595),
(2601,1,0,'Have you returned with the requested organs?',15595),
(2602,1,0,'Have you returned with the requested organs?',15595),
(2603,1,0,'Do not waste my time, $N. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.',15595),
(2604,1,0,'Do not waste my time, $N. We have nothing to discuss, unless you have recovered the items I have requested.',15595),
(2605,1,0,'Please, tell me you found the dew collectors?',15595),
(2606,1,0,'So old Marin\'s up to it again, eh? What\'s this concoction made from?',15595),
(2621,1,0,'',15595),
(2622,1,0,'',15595),
(2623,1,0,'Awaiting orders.',15595),
(2641,1,0,'Under the waters of that lake -- it\'s the only place where the Violet Tragan can be found.  Hope you\'re good at holding your breath!',15595),
(2661,1,0,'Oh, $N, you\'re finally back.  What have you brought?',15595),
(2662,1,0,'',15595),
(2681,1,0,'It is no easy task, $N. Do not give up!',15595),
(2701,1,0,'',15595),
(2702,1,0,'',15595),
(2721,1,0,'',15595),
(2741,1,0,'The Super Egg-O-Matic is the latest of Curgle Cranklehop\'s inventions. It is quite an impressive piece of machinery.$B$BThe Super Egg-O-Matic sputters wildly as you approach the control panel.',15595),
(2742,1,0,'Rin\'ji is scared!',15595),
(2743,1,0,'',15595),
(2744,1,0,'What are you doing here?',15595),
(2745,1,0,'',15595),
(2746,1,0,'I\'ve been watching Lescovar for a couple weeks now. Trias has never trusted him, but we didn\'t suspect he was involved in anything to do with the Defias Brotherhood. We were following leads that tied him to the Twilight\'s Hammer. Either way, he\'s become more dangerous than this city can deal with, and that\'s where we come in.$b$bGet me those items and we can put my plan into effect.',15595),
(2747,1,0,'I have seen very few eggs retrieved from Feralas in extraordinary condition. These are eggs of the rarest sort...',15595),
(2748,1,0,'A fine egg is one that will, in ideal conditions, hatch free of the evil effects of the Gordunni ogres\' incantations.',15595),
(2749,1,0,'Ordinary hippogryph eggs hatch about half the time. We do our best to nurture them and with a little luck, they will hatch.',15595),
(2750,1,0,'These are the eggs that cannot be saved -- they will never hatch.',15595),
(2751,1,0,'Bronze, $N! More bronze!!',15595),
(2752,1,0,'Show me your dedication, $R.',15595),
(2753,1,0,'Their skulls will crack under the pressure of your boots!',15595),
(2754,1,0,'Show the iron who is in charge, $N!',15595),
(2755,1,0,'',15595),
(2766,1,0,'You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken? The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:$b$b\"Yes, excellent work! This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs. Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover - the beacon will take care of the rest!\"',15595),
(2767,1,0,'Yes, I\'m Oglethorpe Obnoticus, master inventor at your service! Now, is there something I could assist you with?',15595),
(2769,1,0,'',15595),
(2781,1,0,'Yes $c, I am an official of the Gadgetzan Water Company.  What can I assist you with?',15595),
(2782,1,0,'Well, now, what is this?',15595),
(2783,1,0,'',15595),
(2784,1,0,'Listen to what I have to say.',15595),
(2801,1,0,'Listen to what I have to say, $N.',15595),
(2821,1,0,'A stack of ten thick yeti hides will net you a choice of one of my crafted items.  Because I care about quality, I am able to ensure you\'ll get a good item!$B$BIf you can\'t seem to find yetis, I know where some might be.  Try looking just inland of the Forgotten Coast, around Feral Scar Vale.',15595),
(2822,1,0,'Were you able to get a stack of ten thick yeti hides? My leather goods are second to none, and I\'ll share a sampling with you should you have the hides.$b$bIf you can\'t seem to find yetis, I know where some might be. Try looking west of here, just inland of the Forgotten Coast around the Feral Scar Vale.',15595),
(2844,1,0,'',15595),
(2845,1,0,'I was gettin\' worried \'bout ya! Thank you so much for bringin\' Shay home, $N.',15595),
(2862,1,0,'We drive them back, and yet they still attack! Someone or something must be driving them into a frenzy... oh, you have returned, eh $N? Do you have the manes I require for the bounty to be met?',15595),
(2863,1,0,'Time is running out, $N! If you\'re not here to report that you\'ve taken out the Alphas, then you\'re wasting time!',15595),
(2866,1,0,'',15595),
(2867,1,0,'',15595),
(2869,1,0,'$N, if you\'re here to verify the task given to you, then excellent - it is ten Hatecrest scales I seek.  If you are here for chit-chat, then I am currently unavailable for such trivialities.$B$BKnow this - we night elves are not warmongers.  Our race is dedicated to the preservation of peace and harmony.  This does not mean, however, that we will not proactively protect our own interests.  This is my duty to General Feathermoon, and to the stronghold.',15595),
(2870,1,0,'Bringing down Lord Shalzaru would certainly set their plans back weeks, if not months.  On top of that, the relic he uncovered is of definite interest to us.$B$BHave you performed the mission given to you, $N?',15595),
(2871,1,0,'Yes, may I assist you?$B$BHold on, you\'re the $C that has been helping General Feathermoon and Latro out with the naga threat, yes?  I\'m Vestia, Latro\'s - erm, rather, Latronicus\' wife.  It is a pleasure to meet you!$B$BI\'m sorry, you\'re here on business, of course.  Do you have something for me - from him, perchance?',15595),
(2872,1,0,'',15595),
(2873,1,0,'Did you find my shipment of rum, $N?',15595),
(2874,1,0,'Did Stoley cough up my booze?',15595),
(2875,1,0,'You look a little dazed.  Have you been reading our legal documents?',15595),
(2876,1,0,'You look out of breath.  You have something to tell me?',15595),
(2877,1,5,'Make no effort to negotiate the mission at hand, $r!  If the gods had wanted those oozes killed, they would have miracled it done by now, wouldn\'t they?!',15595),
(2878,1,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(2879,1,0,'The Equinex Monolith stands silently among the ruins. What could it be holding?',15595),
(2880,5,0,'I want five of those tribal necklaces the trolls carry on them.  If you need it spelled out further, then killing one of them stands you a good chance of getting one!$B$BProve your worth to the Wildhammers!',15595),
(2881,1,0,'I want five of those tribal necklaces the trolls carry on them. If you need it spelled out further, then killing one of them stands you a good chance of getting one!$B$BProve your worth to the Wildhammers!',15595),
(2902,1,0,'',15595),
(2903,1,0,'Welcome back $N - were you able to find some tangible evidence as to the plans of the gnolls?',15595),
(2932,1,0,'You have not completed my task, $N.',15595),
(2933,1,0,'Hello, gentle $C. The day has been long and not a single experiment successful...I hope you bring good news to me.',15595),
(2934,0,0,'Do you have the undamaged venom sac, $N?  I yearn to run experiments with its fresh venom, and have ordered a collection of small, terribly cute animals on which to test it!',15595),
(2935,1,0,'',15595),
(2937,1,0,'Did you get the venom?',15595),
(2938,1,0,'Word was sent of your coming, $N. You have a parcel for me?',15595),
(2939,1,0,'',15595),
(2940,1,0,'',15595),
(2941,1,0,'A letter -- for me?',15595),
(2942,1,0,'I am glad you have returned, $N. I am eager to hear of your findings.',15595),
(2943,1,0,'Hello, $N. Have you been to Darnassus?',15595),
(2944,1,0,'So, you have finally returned, $N. And you\'ve brought the contraption that Curgle built for me -- perfect.',15595),
(2946,1,0,'This familiar looking pedestal sticks out of the hot sand. Perhaps there is something to its presence here...',15595),
(2947,1,0,'Hey, easy there partner - I\'m a very important businessman!  I am sure that the courier is just simply late with the delivery of the rent... wait... you\'re not my landlord.$B$BWell, of course you aren\'t - silly me!  You\'ve come to me seeking the finest jeweler in all of Ironforge, one who does NOT make CURSED items!  Yes!$B$BUm... what do you need?',15595),
(2948,1,0,'Do you have the materials I need?  I wouldn\'t ask you for them if I wasn\'t down on my luck...',15595),
(2949,1,0,'You\'d think that we would find a way on our own to outdo those filthy little gnomes.  I would even wager that they stole that rig from us to begin with!  Bah, those greasy, grimy... erm, yes?  You need something?',15595),
(2950,1,0,'Do you have the materials I need?  I can\'t improve on this design without everything I asked for.',15595),
(2951,1,0,'It would seem that the device needs some sort of grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to get the contraption working. So long as both are present, the Sparklematic 5200 should work...',15595),
(2952,1,0,'',15595),
(2953,1,0,'The Sparklematic 5200 is empty, awaiting a grime-encrusted object to clean and three silver coins to start!',15595),
(2954,1,0,'The purpose of the stone watcher must be learned before continuing on...',15595),
(2963,1,0,'',15595),
(2964,1,0,'',15595),
(2965,1,0,'',15595),
(2966,1,0,'This familiar looking pedestal sticks out of the hot sand.  Perhaps there is something to its presence here...',15595),
(2967,1,0,'Welcome back $N.  Were you able to use the discs to your advantage, or was it for naught?',15595),
(2968,1,0,'',15595),
(2969,1,0,'',15595),
(2970,1,0,'Kindal needs time to prepare, but our kills already number in the dozens. The Grimtotem clan is more than aware of our presence in the area, and they seek us out like vipers.$B$BThey\'ll do everything in their power to take our heads from our bodies. You should be alert... they\'ll be coming for you too now that you\'ve interfered.',15595),
(2972,1,0,'Hello, child. It pleases us to have more powerful adventurers here in the temple. If you have the time, will you share a tale or two with the younger adventurers? I know many of them would benefit from your wisdom.$B$BI\'m sorry, look how rude of me. You\'ve come to the Temple seeking our aid, and I impose on you. Please, forgive me. Tell me what the servants of the Light can do for you.',15595),
(2973,1,0,'The sprite darters can be dangerous critters when provoked. Be careful when dealing with them, $C. And be even more careful of any night elves in the area. The pestering fools tend to hold up in the forests also.$b$bWhen you\'ve gotten enough of the wings, let me know, I\'ll be sure to reward you well!',15595),
(2974,1,0,'Take my words seriously, $C, the Grimtotem clan is evil. If you\'ve found their whereabouts, then it\'s up to you to return and strike the first blow against their clan... before they can come into our own lands and raze our own villages, or pilfer our lands.',15595),
(2975,1,0,'Move swiftly, $N. Or is the task I requested too difficult?',15595),
(2976,1,0,'Be quick, $C, I have much to complete today.',15595),
(2977,1,0,'Welcome back $N.  Were you able to use the discs to your advantage, or did it end up being a wild goose chase?',15595),
(2978,1,0,'What is this?',15595),
(2979,1,0,'We must discover more about why the Gordunni are here, $N.',15595),
(2980,1,0,'Have you found the ruins, $N?',15595),
(2981,1,0,'',15595),
(2982,1,0,'Be watchful around the Gordunni, $N. Their magic seems to wreak havoc on the very land they stand on.',15595),
(2987,1,0,'Get on up there and start digging!$b$bI\'ve got places to go and people to see -- time is money!',15595),
(2988,1,0,'Have you searched the cages, $N? We must find Sharpbeak!',15595),
(2989,1,0,'Hurry, $N!  If the Vilebranch trolls have Sharpbeak, then who knows what they might be doing with him!',15595),
(2990,1,0,'$N, you come bearing a gift?',15595),
(2992,1,0,'',15595),
(2993,1,0,'',15595),
(2994,1,0,'Save Sharpbeak!',15595),
(2995,1,6,'Keeping the Highvale elves isolated is the key. Have you found the lodge?',15595),
(3002,1,0,'What have you brought me, $R?',15595),
(3022,1,0,'Another shipment from Curgle, I assume?',15595),
(3062,1,0,'The hate that Edana spreads across the land must be stopped.',15595),
(3063,1,0,'The wings of the Northspring harpies are black as the night; do not take your eyes off of them, lest they disappear into darkness.',15595),
(3087,2,0,'Ah, so you come at last. Good. Jen\'shan be waitin\' for you.$B$BMany tink it be an easy path, but Jen\'shan tell you dat not true. Mastering da beasts of Durotar and beyond take as much skill as masterin\' the arcane arts or speakin\' to our ancestors.$B$BFirin\' a bow or rifle may not be as dangerous to you as castin\' a spell, but it sure be as dangerous to your enemy.',15595),
(3088,2,5,'Shhh, not so loud. I don\'t trust Nartok over there. Anyone that has to hide deeper in a cave than I do shouldn\'t be trifled with.$b$bI trust you had no problem finding your way around?',15595),
(3089,2,0,'So, you\'ve arrived. I was beginning to wonder when you would show yourself. I sent the parchment some time ago--I wasn\'t sure if it had arrived.$B$BBut enough chatter... you\'re here because you have been chosen, chosen to lead the spiritual lives of our people.',15595),
(3090,1,0,'Finally, you\'ve arrived... and discretely also. Good.$b$bOur world is full of fools, Asatokta. Even the mighty Thrall has greater flaws than most can see. He turns his back on the power needed to make this land ours completely! We\'re not the same people who were manipulated and used by creatures from the Nether. We are our own people. We are proud... and we are strong.',15595),
(3091,1,0,'Ah, at last, you\'ve arrived, $c. I did not lie in my note, $N. We are a special breed also, not unlike the druids or shamans of our tribe. You are just as important. We are the ones called upon to defend our borders, to hunt the centaur, and to go to war.',15595),
(3092,1,0,'Welcome to Camp Narache, $n. I hear good things about you. Your bloodline is strong, and many of the elders consider you skilled already. But that we will test.$b$bThe plains of Mulgore will be your home for sometime--you should do your best to learn it very well. One day you will travel to unfamilar lands to master greater skills. You must be ready.',15595),
(3093,1,0,'As quickly as water falls from the sky, here you are before me. I am pleased by your haste. It means you realize both the importance of our meeting and you being here. I am no leader, but I do understand the elements, and I can speak to the spirits of our people. I will teach you to do the same.',15595),
(3094,1,0,'You have arrived. This is good. Our ancestors\' spirits have become restless throughout Mulgore and beyond, but I cannot tell why. It will forever be your duty to learn to listen to nature\'s spirits, and act as their avatar. Be mindful of that.',15595),
(3095,1,0,'Ah, so you\'ve arrived. Good. I overheard that a few others were able to escape \"death\" and were heading into town. Perhaps that resilence will pay off in the future also.$B$BYou may thank Sylvanas for your freedom... freedom of mind and body. Though you still remain tortured by the plague and its effects, you are now free to come and go as you see fit.',15595),
(3096,1,0,'So you\'ve made it? Good, we\'ll have need of more rogues as time goes on. The Shadowstalkers will probably wind up finding you when they think the time\'s right, so don\'t go and slip up or do anything you might regret. They need talented agents... not pickpockets and fools.',15595),
(3097,1,0,'Ah, so between fire, plague, rioting, and much worse, one more of the \"faithful\" comes to my door. Well, let me bid you welcome, $C. And allow me a moment to explain a thing or two before you decide it\'s time for you to seek whatever drives you forward: the Holy Light no longer concerns you, the spirits of your forefathers are fairy tales, and creatures from the Nether don\'t want you.$b$bDo you understand me so far?',15595),
(3098,1,0,'I knew you would come to me, $N. Not because you do not have the will to follow your own path, but because we are kindred spirits. We both have felt pain. We have both suffered. And now we want the power to take back what we know is ours: this land, our lives, our destinies. But there is much for you to learn still.',15595),
(3099,1,0,'I bid you welcome, $gbrother:sister;. I knew you would come. It was only a matter of time.$b$bWhat I said interested you, didn\'t it? I hit a chord... something inside you knew what I claimed was truth. Good.$b$bKnow this though: I am no traitor to Sylvanas. If anything, she would appreciate my claims considering it was her own beliefs that has put the Forsaken in the position it is now.',15595),
(3100,2,0,'Ah, you got my letter, $N... good.$B$BThere\'s been an influx of warriors in Elwynn recently - which is good for Stormwind, but bad for the kobolds and Defias in the area.',15595),
(3101,4,0,'Finally! We meet face to face, brother to brother. I welcome you to Northshire. This will be your home for a short time while you learn the ins and outs of how things are done, but know that Stormwind is not far off, and sooner or later, your path will take you there. But until then, be patient... Knight of the Silver Hand.',15595),
(3102,2,0,'You made it here in one piece, and it doesn\'t look like too many people saw you. Good enough for me. I don\'t like to have much attention drawn to me back here... nice and quiet. I\'m sure you can understand.$B$BHave any trouble yet? I\'m glad to hear not. That\'ll change soon enough.',15595),
(3103,2,0,'Ah, at last you\'ve come. I knew you would find your way to me. The Holy Light shines upon you, and the path you\'ve chosen. These times are harsh--the Burning Legion still has a presence upon Azeroth, the entirety of Kalimdor seeks new ways to defend itself from its own tribulations, and it is up to you to aid as many as you can.',15595),
(3104,6,0,'Hello, $N. I am Khelden. Is there something I can do for you?',15595),
(3105,1,0,'Ah, so you\'ve arrived, and not a moment too soon, $N. Some of the guards were over here a moment ago and were giving me curious looks... pathetic mundanes.',15595),
(3106,6,0,'Blast it\'s cold today, aint it? It\'s like the snow never goes away, $N.$b$bYou\'ve probably noticed already, but there are gnomes now living in our city. That\'s because they went and got themselves blown out of their own home. Don\'t go spreadin\' this \'round, but I can hardly blame them--I think I woulda resorted to explosives too if Ironforge were infested with Dark Irons or the like.',15595),
(3107,1,0,'So, you\'ve made it! And not a second too soon. There\'s much to be done in Coldridge Valley and beyond. I\'m gonna need your help as much as you\'re gonna need mine!$B$BYou\'re a Knight of the Silver Hand now, be ready to play the part.',15595),
(3108,4,0,'Ya made it! Good to hear! Betcha didn\'t have to track me to find the place either. Haha!',15595),
(3109,2,0,'You made it! Great!$B$BWe\'ve got an influx of activity lately, so I\'m glad to count another of the Ironforge clan among our numbers. Too many of us are lookin\' to the arcane, and divine for my own tastes. Nothin\' against them and their beliefs, but there\'s nothing like a cold blade in your hand and a shadow to keep you from the light, know what I mean?',15595),
(3110,6,0,'Ach! Ya made it, $N! Wonderful!$B$BI was gonna say, I was about to lose faith that ye\'d arrive at all... get it, lose faith? It\'s a joke, lass... aww, nevermind. Ya didn\'t come here for me bad jokes anyway.',15595),
(3115,1,0,'Wonderful! You got my memorandum obviously.$b$bIgnore the fools around you, $N. The Holy Light?! The sword and shield?! These aren\'t paths for ones as open minded as us. Look at what \"normal\" magic did to our home. Coupled with those damned tinkerers, our race almost became extinct. And now we have to rely on the dwarves-- they\'d rather spend time allying with humans than help us rebuild our own home. We\'re like second-class citizens. Have you seen the way they look at us?',15595),
(3116,1,0,'You made it. I\'m so glad.$b$bMuch has happened over the last few years, $N: the creation of Teldrassil, the corruption of many of the forest creatures here and abroad, discovery of lands we thought lost to us like Feralas... so much, in so little time. But those are just some of the reasons we are here, the most important being to protect our kind from further evil.',15595),
(3117,1,0,'You\'ve arrived, and none too soon, $N. Welcome to Shadowglen.$B$BI trust my sigil found you in good spirits and health?$B$BAs I said previously, I am here to train you as a $C; to tame beasts to aid you in battle; to use a bow with unerring accuracy; to respect the lands which we call home and also the lands beyond.',15595),
(3118,2,1,'Hello, Ferlis. I\'m glad you found me. I was thinking that perhaps you got lost on the way here.$b$bNothing really new has happened in Shadowglen since I sent you my sigil, but I\'ll leave all the information gathering to you. Speak to the rest of the people around Aldrassil if you\'d like.',15595),
(3119,1,0,'It pleases me to see you\'ve arrived so quickly, $N. Welcome.$b$bAs you\'ve probably heard, all of Teldrassil is stirring with the comings and goings of travelers. Even members of the Alliance have even been allowed access onto Teldrassil\'s boughs in order to meet with other Kaldorei who prepare for the adventures ahead.',15595),
(3120,1,0,'Ah, young $c. I see you\'re eager to continue your studies. Good.$B$BI wonder, have you spent much time in the Emerald Dream already? Perhaps you\'re not prepared for that yet... In time, I\'m sure.$B$BBut until then, we should discuss other matters.',15595),
(3121,1,0,'Yes?',15595),
(3122,1,0,'Have you spoken to Neeru?',15595),
(3123,1,0,'Were you able to capture the wildkin?$b$bIf you succeed, we will be ready to shrink and capture the muisek of creatures of Feralas.',15595),
(3124,1,0,'Were you able to capture the hippogryphs?',15595),
(3125,1,0,'Were you able to capture the muisek of the faerie dragons?',15595),
(3126,1,0,'Were you able to capture the wandering forest walkers?',15595),
(3127,1,0,'Were you able to capture the mountain giants?',15595),
(3128,1,0,'Were you able to collect the materials I need?',15595),
(3129,1,0,'',15595),
(3130,1,0,'',15595),
(3141,1,0,'Do not interrupt me, $r.',15595),
(3161,1,0,'Are you having any trouble?$B$BYou can find Gahz\'ridian just about anywhere in Tanaris, $N, so keep looking!',15595),
(3181,1,0,'No, I will not open the gate.',15595),
(3182,1,0,'Why hello there young lady. Would you like a tour of the museum?',15595),
(3201,1,0,'I don\'t believe it.',15595),
(3221,1,0,'',15595),
(3261,1,0,'',15595),
(3281,1,0,'Do you have the silver?',15595),
(3301,1,0,'I can smell the dust of the Barrens on you, $C. You have traveled far.',15595),
(3341,1,0,'This matter is of utmost importance, $N. We must stop any attempt by the Scourge to bolster their ranks.',15595),
(3361,0,0,'Once I get my tools, I\'m outta here.',15595),
(3362,1,0,'I\'d like to take a closer look at that cactus in the valley... So leave some of it in one piece, will ya?',15595),
(3363,1,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant. A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
(3366,1,0,NULL,15595),
(3367,1,0,'I\'m not going to make it...',15595),
(3368,1,0,'<Thorius sobs.>',15595),
(3369,1,0,'May I help you with something?',15595),
(3370,1,0,'May I help you with something?',15595),
(3371,1,0,'',15595),
(3372,1,0,'The altar is empty.',15595),
(3374,1,0,'Here we are $N, at yet another crossroads. The time has come to make another choice. What choice do you make, mortal?',15595),
(3377,1,0,'Allow me to finish my story.',15595),
(3378,1,0,'What brings you to the Temple of the Moon, $N?',15595),
(3381,1,0,'I remain here at my master\'s bidding. I\'ve been given leave to ask any price I wish for transportation up to his tower. For now, I ask for only the two feathers from each traveler so I can continue to make my signature arrows.$b$bIf you\'re not careful, I\'ll up the price. How does half a dozen gold sound?$b$bYeah, I thought as much. Just mind yourself and I\'ll keep the price where it is.',15595),
(3382,1,0,'Have you met with Andron yet? He rarely leaves Undercity, so I don\'t think it\'d be too hard to find him.',15595),
(3421,1,0,'',15595),
(3441,1,0,'Allow me to finish mo... $r.',15595),
(3442,1,0,'Have you collected the materials?',15595),
(3443,1,0,'Eight, $N. I need eight!	',15595),
(3444,1,0,'Ratchet is not far from here, $N. The journey shouldn\'t take long.',15595),
(3445,1,0,'',15595),
(3448,1,0,'',15595),
(3449,4,0,'Well, well, well, glad to see you made it out here, $N. Did you get the rubbings for Tymor?$B$BAs dangerous as this place is, there hasn\'t been too much action along the coast. That might be on account of the naga swimming underwater, but that\'s not my problem... I patrol the skies.',15595),
(3450,1,0,'',15595),
(3451,1,0,'',15595),
(3452,0,0,'Without a suitable source of arcane energy, the torch of retribution cannot be completed.',15595),
(3453,1,0,'Do not interrupt the channeling process.',15595),
(3454,1,0,'',15595),
(3461,6,0,'You\'re back! Excellent. Do you have my drawing kit also?',15595),
(3462,1,0,'',15595),
(3463,1,0,'Are you lost, $N?',15595),
(3481,1,0,'',15595),
(3483,1,0,NULL,15595),
(3501,1,0,'Have you had any luck in your exploration?',15595),
(3502,1,0,'Well? Draenethyst? Remember?$B$B<Kum\'isha clenches his fist and knocks on your head.>$B$BIs anybody home?',15595),
(3503,1,0,'',15595),
(3504,1,0,'Ah, Belgrom wizened up and finally sent someone not in his ranks to aid us, did he?$b$bThis camp used to be a dozen warriors strong, $N, but now they\'re all dead. That $C, Rimtori, has slain them all. She played Belgrom like a lute... seduced him even. It\'s none of my business, but between you and I, she is quite the temptress. That\'s probably why I\'m still out here helping Belgrom--I probably would have done the same thing.',15595),
(3505,1,0,'The title of the book is emblazoned on the black leather cover in gold leaf--Kaldorei Tome of Summoning. As you open the pages you can see that the book is very old but in superb condition.$b$bYou assume the text is of some ancient language... perhaps Kaldorei?$b$bYour instincts tell you that you should return here once you\'ve finished doling out retribution on the blood elves for their betrayal.',15595),
(3506,1,0,'How goes your slaughter of the blood elf traitors, $N? Have you made any progress?$b$bI hope you are the one strong enough to bring that dog to her knees! She deserves nothing but a painful death for all that she has done!',15595),
(3507,1,0,'I remember you, $C. I asked you to go to Azshara to destroy that wench that betrayed me! That seems like many moons ago. Don\'t tell me that Ag\'tor and the others are dead also!',15595),
(3508,1,0,'',15595),
(3509,1,0,'',15595),
(3510,1,0,'<Lord Arkkoroc bends down to inspect you.>$b$bWhere are they?',15595),
(3511,1,0,'You return! Astounding, $R. Did you discover the true name?$b$b',15595),
(3512,1,0,'',15595),
(3513,1,0,'Whaddya got?',15595),
(3514,1,0,'We cannot allow the Alliance on our land, $N. Make this known.',15595),
(3517,1,0,'The tablets I\'m having you gather should bring in a pretty copper or two to the right parties. I\'ll tell you who we need to deliver them to after you\'ve found them. But I\'m no fool... you\'ll get your share after I have proof that they\'ve been delivered.$b$bSo get to it--we don\'t have all day. I might have to find someone else to help me.',15595),
(3518,1,0,'Yes, $N. What can I do for you? I have many matters I must attend to, so please, be quick.',15595),
(3520,0,0,'Have you collected the essence of the screecher spirits, $N?',15595),
(3523,1,0,'I\'m not one for politics; I care not if your affiliations are for either Horde or Alliance.  I am more interested in squelching direct and dire threats to all the races... and we have quite a large one in here.$B$BIf you\'re willing to be a true hero for all people, then hand me the oathstone I have given you as a sign of commitment.  I\'m... not from around these parts; an oathstone is important to people of my kind as a bond of agreement.',15595),
(3524,1,0,'It is only recently that these creatures started landing on the coast of Darkshore in such alarming numbers. I can\'t help but think that this is an ill omen of some sort. Recovering a sample of that creature\'s bones to the south would help us in Darnassus assess this situation!',15595),
(3525,1,0,'',15595),
(3541,1,0,'Yes, what you be needin\', $gdad:mon? I got many tings to be takin\' care of today, and you not be on me agenda as one of them. Pester me, and I make sure that changes.',15595),
(3542,1,0,'Well... ... isn\'t this a surprise? An adventurererere... !$b$bWhat c\'n I do for you... ?',15595),
(3561,1,0,'What can help you with, $N?',15595),
(3562,1,0,'Well, what did Magatha say? The old crone... I bet she was less than polite.',15595),
(3563,1,0,'Have you spoken to Jes\'rimon yet?$B$BHe\'s a boar among trolls, but his information is usually accurate and his jobs well paying.$B$BIf you can stand his attitude then you stand to make some good coin from his business endeavors.',15595),
(3564,1,0,'Have you met with Andron yet? He rarely leaves Undercity, so I don\'t think it\'d be too hard to find him.',15595),
(3565,1,0,'Well, what did Xylem have to say? He didn\'t do anything to you, did he? Cast a spell on you? Con you into doing work for him?',15595),
(3566,1,0,'I don\'t believe you! Show me proof!',15595),
(3567,1,0,'',15595),
(3568,6,0,'You know where this is leading, don\'t you, $N? There\'s no way she can survive... look at her. The best thing for her now is to aid us in finding a cure for the plague. This water she drank might have a clue that helps us figure out how. She\'s going to die anyway--she might as well die doing something noble for our people before she does. Don\'t you agree?',15595),
(3569,1,0,'I\'ve come to Undercity because I heard their alchemists have been studying long and hard on how to find a cure for their own illness. It was suggested that perhaps they could help me too.$B$BAlthough this place makes me feel far from welcome, I had no choice--the sickness that found me is tearing me up inside and I needed their help immediately.',15595),
(3570,1,0,'You know where this is leading, don\'t you, $N? There\'s no way she can survive... look at her. The best thing for her now is to aid us in finding a cure for the plague. This water she drank might have a clue that helps us figure out how. She\'s going to die anyway--she might as well die doing something noble for our people before she does. Don\'t you agree?',15595),
(3601,14,0,'Those stinkin\' Blood elves. I tell ya, if I was as strong as you are, I\'d go down there and teach them a thing or two myself! But I\'ll have to settle with payin\' you to take care of \'em for me.',15595),
(3602,1,0,'Evil does not sleep, fool. You will have time for rest when you are finally dead. Now, bring me those crystals.',15595),
(3621,1,0,'Loramus, eh? It has been many years since I have heard that name.',15595),
(3625,1,0,'To interrupt the forging process could result in an imperfect weapon. Be patient, $n.',15595),
(3626,1,0,'',15595),
(3627,1,0,'The three shall form the one, the one shall light the way.',15595),
(3628,1,0,'There is nothing left to fear.$b$b',15595),
(3630,1,0,'Yes, yes, what needs of yours might I address today? Clearly, I have the time to do such since all I do is stand here while our beloved city lies in a cloud of irradiated death.',15595),
(3636,1,0,'Amnennar must be eradicated. Go, swiftly.',15595),
(3701,1,0,'Do you bring new information?',15595),
(3702,1,0,'Allow me to finish telling you the story of Thaurissan.',15595),
(3721,1,0,'',15595),
(3741,1,0,'Hi. I miss my necklace. My daddy got it for me. Daddy says that there are monsters in the lake. Did you beat up any monsters?',15595),
(3761,1,0,'At ease, Private. If you\'re here to unload soil from Un\'Goro - outstanding then! Otherwise, disappear.',15595),
(3762,1,0,'',15595),
(3763,1,0,'',15595),
(3764,1,0,'Ah yes, the dirt. The Arch Druid wants twenty loads per adventurer, and twenty loads he shall get. Let those who conspire against us fall to the wayside!',15595),
(3765,1,0,'',15595),
(3781,1,0,'Peace and serenity be yours, friend. You are here on business from the Arch Druid himself, yes?',15595),
(3782,1,0,'Peace and serenity be yours, friend. You are here on business from the Arch Druid himself, yes?',15595),
(3783,1,0,'I\'ve got lots to get started on here. Please get me those furs as soon as you can!',15595),
(3784,1,0,'',15595),
(3785,1,0,'Yes $N, have you grown some morrowgrain for the Arch Druid\'s important research? The mysterious properties of Un\'Goro Crater become clearer with each passing day, thanks to the help you are giving us.',15595),
(3786,6,0,'Yes $N, have you grown some morrowgrain for the Arch Druid\'s important research?  The mysterious properties of Un\'Goro Crater become clearer with each passing day, thanks to the help you are giving us.',15595),
(3787,1,0,'',15595),
(3789,1,0,'',15595),
(3790,1,0,'',15595),
(3801,1,0,'',15595),
(3802,0,0,'The statue looms ominously above you.',15595),
(3803,1,0,'The Arch Druid is always looking for additional morrowgrain for the Cenarion Circle\'s continued research. We take them in increments of ten, and award you with a cache of goods you should find useful. When you have ten, let me know and I will reward you accordingly.',15595),
(3804,1,0,'The Arch Druid is always looking for more morrowgrain for the Cenarion Circle\'s research project on Un\'Goro Crater. We take them in increments of ten, and award you with a cache of goods you should find useful. When you have ten, let me know and I will award you accordingly.',15595),
(3821,1,0,'',15595),
(3822,1,0,'Did you find Sha\'ni? Is she ok?',15595),
(3823,1,0,'There is not nearly enough blood on your uniform, soldier!',15595),
(3824,1,0,'Oh glorious day! Have you returned with the head?',15595),
(3825,1,0,'So? Did you paint any pictures of the event?',15595),
(3841,1,0,'Why hello, $C.$B$BDon\'t let my location fool you, I\'m really not here for the races... as entertaining as they may be.$B$BI\'m actually here in Thousand Needles investigating all I can to find out how salvageable the land is. It has become my crusade of sorts to revitalize and replenish the area with new, fertile soil. Perhaps I\'ll find there\'s a water source nearby.$B$BTell me you haven\'t noticed how odd the transition between Feralas and Thousand Needles is. Strange magic was afoot when that happened.',15595),
(3842,1,0,'The longer I stay here, the more tempted I am to partake in these races, $N. Truly boggling...$B$BHave you found the elixirs yet? Once I can tell if the egg is going to be healthy or not, I\'ll return it to you to hold onto until it\'s prepared to hatch.$B$BLet me know.',15595),
(3843,1,0,'Greetin\'s, $N. How can I be of service to ya?',15595),
(3844,1,0,'',15595),
(3845,1,0,'Hi there. I\'ve seen you before... Haven\'t I?',15595),
(3861,1,0,'The chicken stares at you with dark, cold eyes. It waits for you hungrily.$B$B\"BACAAAW!$B$BCluck...cluck...cluck.\"',15595),
(3881,1,0,'If we\'re going to have any chance of getting out of here alive, we\'ll need our big crate of foodstuffs.  Also, getting at least some of our research equipment back would be a blessing in a sea of misery.',15595),
(3882,1,0,'Think whatever you want of me, but they\'re not going to care if the bones they get to research are from ones from ancient stegodons and diemetradons or the ones that almost devoured us wholesale when we were trying to set up our camps.  I\'ll just be happy if we get out of here alive...',15595),
(3883,6,0,'Do you have the sample of the Gorishi hive for me to study, $N?',15595),
(3884,3,0,'Hello there!  I and my companions are happy to see some living beings here other than overgrown savage beasts!  What brings you into the Un\'Goro Crater?',15595),
(3906,1,0,'The elements are still in disarray, $N.',15595),
(3907,1,0,'The flames will soon overtake these lands. Make haste, $N!$b$b',15595),
(3908,1,0,'My, my... So Linken did finally get around to sending me his sword.',15595),
(3909,1,0,'Back already?',15595),
(3911,1,0,'Show them to me!',15595),
(3912,1,0,NULL,15595),
(3913,1,0,'This must be the gravestone that Gaeriyan mentioned...',15595),
(3914,1,0,'Oh! I remember you! You are... No, don\'t tell me!',15595),
(3921,1,0,'I\'m very busy with my work, $C. Unless you have something for me, it\'d be best if you moved along...',15595),
(3922,1,0,'Do you have the nugget slugs, $N? I\'ve been eyeing this Samophlange and I can\'t wait to tinker with it.',15595),
(3923,1,0,'Mind your head! I don\'t want it to get in the way of my work!',15595),
(3924,1,0,'Do you have the manual?',15595),
(3941,1,0,'',15595),
(3942,1,0,'',15595),
(3961,1,0,'Hi, again, $N!',15595),
(3962,1,0,'Blazerunner is almost invincible behind the aura he has created by using the Golden Flame. Only you have the power to remove it with the Silver Totem of Aquementas.',15595),
(3981,1,0,'',15595),
(3982,1,0,'Defend yourself, fool!',15595),
(4001,1,0,'What brings you to these hallowed grounds?',15595),
(4002,1,0,'',15595),
(4003,1,0,'<Princess Moira cowers in fear.>',15595),
(4004,1,0,'',15595),
(4005,1,0,'So you\'re back, eh? Hmm... Let me take a look at that, $N.',15595),
(4021,1,0,'Do you have the banner?',15595),
(4022,1,0,'<Cyrus\'s eyes form two blazing spheres.>',15595),
(4023,1,0,'<Cyrus\'s eyes form two blazing spheres.>',15595),
(4024,6,0,'Has the giant been felled?',15595),
(4041,1,0,'Bring me an Evoroot, and sure, I can make ya that Videre Elixir.$B$BI know all kinds of things about herbs and alchemy... Why, let me tell you the story about the time I transmuted gold from the cheese I was going to eat for lunch... hey... Where are you going?',15595),
(4061,1,0,'Do not take this task lightly, $N!',15595),
(4062,1,0,'What have you got there, $R?',15595),
(4063,1,0,'Was it him? Was he really alive?',15595),
(4081,1,6,'What is it, $r? Can\'t you see I have a platoon to command?$B$B',15595),
(4082,1,0,'You again? I have to hand it to you, $N, you are tenacious.',15595),
(4083,1,0,'The gems make no sound as they fall into depths of the chalice... ',15595),
(4084,1,0,'I can tell you more of the power of which you required to defeat Blazerunner, but first, you need to gather the things I require.',15595),
(4101,1,0,'I know Felwood suffers, $N - I suffer along with it!  I must remain steadfast in my conviction; were the knowledge I possess to fall into the wrong hands, it would spell disaster for all of Felwood.$B$BBring to me the blood amber drawn from the slain Warpwood elementals, and I will trust you enough to help me enact a means to fight the corruption.',15595),
(4102,1,0,'I know Felwood suffers, $N - I suffer along with it!  I must remain steadfast in my conviction; were the knowledge I possess to fall into the wrong hands, it would spell disaster for all of Felwood.$B$BBring to me the blood amber drawn from the slain Warpwood elementals, and I will trust you enough to help me enact a means to fight the corruption.',15595),
(4103,1,0,'Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to sea a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.$b$bIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.',15595),
(4104,1,0,'If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.$b$bIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I\'ll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.',15595),
(4105,1,0,'A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood\'s corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.$b$bWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.',15595),
(4106,1,0,'A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!$b$bWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.',15595),
(4107,1,0,'The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I\'ve devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don\'t need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.$b$bI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!',15595),
(4108,1,0,'Possessing a Cenarion Beacon allows one to sea a corrupted soul shard on those tainted beasts that are put down for the greater good. I grind shards into a usable reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. We will use that salve to turn corrupted plants into healthy ones again.$b$bIn exchange for these shards, I will give you some Cenarion plant salves I have already prepared.',15595),
(4109,1,0,'If you possess a Cenarion beacon while mining in Felwood, you will be able to see tainted vitriol that corrupts a vein of raw metal. I know how to purify that vitriol and turn it into a reagent that goes into making Cenarion plant salve. You will then use that salve on plants you find in the wild that need saving.$b$bIf you have collected any tainted vitriol, I\'ll give you some Cenarion plant salve I have already prepared.',15595),
(4110,1,0,'A Cenarion beacon allows a seasoned herbalist to spot insidious fel creep - a malfeasant product of Felwood\'s corruption. My work here has taught me the knowledge of purifying fel creep into a cleansing reagent... used in what we now refer to as Cenarion plant salve.$b$bWhen you gather herbs in Felwood, you should encounter the fel creep so long as you have the beacon. In exchange for what you bring to me, I will give you pre-made Cenarion plant salve.',15595),
(4111,1,0,'A Cenarion beacon will allow a well-trained skinner to spot patches of tainted skin from bounty gathered in Felwood. I convert these seemingly useless patches into a thick paste that serves as a quickening agent for Cenarion plant salve. When you skin your kills here in Felwood, be sure to have a beacon on you!$b$bWhen you collect tainted patches, bring them to me and I will give you some Cenarion plant salves that I have already made.',15595),
(4112,1,0,'The power of a disenchanted magical item is felt by the essence it creates. I\'ve devised a way to turn raw essence used by enchanters into a suitable reagent for creating Cenarion plant salve. You don\'t need a Cenarion beacon for this; any suitably disenchanted item that yields lesser nether essences will work.$b$bI just need a single lesser nether essence; in exchange, I will give you Cenarion plant salves. The essence is extremely potent - a little definitely goes a long way!',15595),
(4113,0,0,'You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a songflower plant.  A pungent, unhealthy odor emanates from the plant.  It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.',15595),
